{
 "p012": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 5.52,
   "end_s": 6.94,
   "dur_s": 1.42,
   "text": "What’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 7.8,
   "end_s": 8.51,
   "dur_s": 0.71,
   "text": "I’m Flavia."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 10.34,
   "end_s": 11.54,
   "dur_s": 1.2,
   "text": "Where are you from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 12.36,
   "end_s": 16.335,
   "dur_s": 3.975,
   "text": "I’m from Brazil. I live in Fortaleza."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 18.16,
   "end_s": 19.679,
   "dur_s": 1.519,
   "text": "How old are you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 20.26,
   "end_s": 20.697,
   "dur_s": 0.437,
   "text": "I’m 11."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 20.72,
   "end_s": 25.2,
   "dur_s": 4.48,
   "text": "Who are your favourite musicians?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 25.82,
   "end_s": 30.685,
   "dur_s": 4.865,
   "text": "Blackpink. They’re a girl group from South Korea."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 32.52,
   "end_s": 34.98,
   "dur_s": 2.46,
   "text": "Why are they your favourite musicians?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 35.54,
   "end_s": 36.96,
   "dur_s": 1.42,
   "text": "Because they’re great!"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 39.66,
   "end_s": 41.273,
   "dur_s": 1.613,
   "text": "What’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 41.86,
   "end_s": 43.5,
   "dur_s": 1.64,
   "text": "My name is Jess."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 45.62,
   "end_s": 46.68,
   "dur_s": 1.06,
   "text": "Where are you from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 47.28,
   "end_s": 51.06,
   "dur_s": 3.78,
   "text": "I’m British. I’m from Newcastle."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 52.9,
   "end_s": 54.37,
   "dur_s": 1.47,
   "text": "How old are you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 54.37,
   "end_s": 55.48,
   "dur_s": 1.11,
   "text": "I’m 12."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 57.32,
   "end_s": 59.44,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "Who’s your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 60.244,
   "end_s": 64.16,
   "dur_s": 3.916,
   "text": "Bruno Mars. He’s a singer from the US."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 66.26,
   "end_s": 68.5,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "Why is he your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 69.08,
   "end_s": 70.9,
   "dur_s": 1.82,
   "text": "Because he’s awesome!"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 73.7,
   "end_s": 75.1,
   "dur_s": 1.4,
   "text": "What’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 108.6,
   "end_s": 110.74,
   "dur_s": 2.14,
   "text": "My name is Li Jun."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 112.44,
   "end_s": 113.8,
   "dur_s": 1.36,
   "text": "Where are you from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 114.48,
   "end_s": 118.64,
   "dur_s": 4.16,
   "text": "I’m from Indonesia. I live in Jakarta."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 120.64,
   "end_s": 122.067,
   "dur_s": 1.427,
   "text": "How old are you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 122.613,
   "end_s": 123.64,
   "dur_s": 1.027,
   "text": "I’m 11."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 125.3,
   "end_s": 127.52,
   "dur_s": 2.22,
   "text": "Who’s your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 128.16,
   "end_s": 132.14,
   "dur_s": 3.98,
   "text": "Yuja Wang. She’s a pianist from China."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 134.14,
   "end_s": 136.28,
   "dur_s": 2.14,
   "text": "Why is she your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 136.98,
   "end_s": 137.797,
   "dur_s": 0.817,
   "text": "Because she’s cool!"
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 137.84,
   "end_s": 138.04,
   "dur_s": 0.2,
   "text": "What’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "start_s": 138.14,
   "end_s": 138.19,
   "dur_s": 0.05,
   "text": "Cenc."
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "start_s": 138.29,
   "end_s": 138.59,
   "dur_s": 0.3,
   "text": "Where are you from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "start_s": 138.59,
   "end_s": 138.665,
   "dur_s": 0.075,
   "text": "I’m Turkish. I’m from a city called Izmir."
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "start_s": 138.665,
   "end_s": 138.703,
   "dur_s": 0.038,
   "text": "How old are you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "start_s": 138.703,
   "end_s": 138.722,
   "dur_s": 0.019,
   "text": "I’m ten."
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "start_s": 138.722,
   "end_s": 138.731,
   "dur_s": 0.009,
   "text": "Who’s your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 37,
   "start_s": 138.731,
   "end_s": 138.736,
   "dur_s": 0.005,
   "text": "Ed Sheeran. He’s a singer and a guitar player."
  },
  {
   "i": 38,
   "start_s": 138.736,
   "end_s": 138.738,
   "dur_s": 0.002,
   "text": "Why is he your favourite musician?"
  },
  {
   "i": 39,
   "start_s": 138.738,
   "end_s": 138.939,
   "dur_s": 0.201,
   "text": "Because he’s great!"
  }
 ],
 "p015": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.08,
   "end_s": 10.54,
   "dur_s": 4.46,
   "text": "Hello and welcome to the One Minute Challenge."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 13.2,
   "end_s": 18.02,
   "dur_s": 4.82,
   "text": "On Line 1 we have Jason. Where are you from, Jason?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.72,
   "end_s": 20.92,
   "dur_s": 2.2,
   "text": "Hi, Megan. I'm from Birmingham."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 21.4,
   "end_s": 26.6,
   "dur_s": 5.2,
   "text": "That's great. OK, Jason, you have one minute."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 27.36,
   "end_s": 29.38,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "How many questions can you answer?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 30.0,
   "end_s": 36.38,
   "dur_s": 6.38,
   "text": "Today's questions are all about nationalities. OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 37.46,
   "end_s": 39.38,
   "dur_s": 1.92,
   "text": "Jason, are you ready?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 40.0,
   "end_s": 41.02,
   "dur_s": 1.02,
   "text": "Yes, I am."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 41.6,
   "end_s": 44.92,
   "dur_s": 3.32,
   "text": "So let's play the One Minute Challenge."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 46.84,
   "end_s": 47.76,
   "dur_s": 0.92,
   "text": "OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 49.1,
   "end_s": 53.14,
   "dur_s": 4.04,
   "text": "Coco Goff, the tennis player, is from..."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 53.14,
   "end_s": 56.6,
   "dur_s": 3.46,
   "text": "The US. She's American. Correct."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 57.48,
   "end_s": 58.52,
   "dur_s": 1.04,
   "text": "Question 2."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 59.02,
   "end_s": 61.26,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "Pyea is from..."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 61.26,
   "end_s": 65.94,
   "dur_s": 4.68,
   "text": "Pyea? That's a type of food. It's South African."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 66.54,
   "end_s": 74.88,
   "dur_s": 8.34,
   "text": "No, I'm sorry. You're wrong. It's a Spanish dish. Of course. Three."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 76.0,
   "end_s": 78.82,
   "dur_s": 2.82,
   "text": "Cape Town is a city in..."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 78.82,
   "end_s": 82.02,
   "dur_s": 3.2,
   "text": "South Africa. It's a South African city."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 82.86,
   "end_s": 85.42,
   "dur_s": 2.56,
   "text": "Correct. Next question."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 86.92,
   "end_s": 90.16,
   "dur_s": 3.24,
   "text": "Cariocas are people from..."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 90.96,
   "end_s": 92.3,
   "dur_s": 1.34,
   "text": "I have no idea."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 93.24,
   "end_s": 97.58,
   "dur_s": 4.34,
   "text": "Cariocas. They're from Rio de Janeiro in Brazil."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 98.32,
   "end_s": 99.5,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "I didn't know that."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 100.7,
   "end_s": 105.64,
   "dur_s": 4.94,
   "text": "The actor, Yalitza Aparicio, is from..."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 105.64,
   "end_s": 107.0,
   "dur_s": 1.36,
   "text": "Spain, I think."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 107.72,
   "end_s": 111.14,
   "dur_s": 3.42,
   "text": "Sorry, you're wrong. She's Mexican."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 112.16,
   "end_s": 113.26,
   "dur_s": 1.1,
   "text": "Last question."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 114.22,
   "end_s": 116.34,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "Salsa music is..."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 118.62,
   "end_s": 122.22,
   "dur_s": 3.6,
   "text": "I'm sorry, Jason. We're out of time."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 123.14,
   "end_s": 125.4,
   "dur_s": 2.26,
   "text": "Your score is 2."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 125.96,
   "end_s": 127.4,
   "dur_s": 1.44,
   "text": "Oh, terrible."
  }
 ],
 "p016": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.42,
   "end_s": 7.2,
   "dur_s": 0.78,
   "text": "Nice T-shirt."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 8.1,
   "end_s": 11.02,
   "dur_s": 2.92,
   "text": "Thank you. It’s Ariana Grande."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 11.64,
   "end_s": 17.4,
   "dur_s": 5.76,
   "text": "I know. I’m an Ariana Grande fan, too. So, what’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 18.24,
   "end_s": 21.049,
   "dur_s": 2.809,
   "text": ". And what’s your name?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 21.48,
   "end_s": 22.26,
   "dur_s": 0.78,
   "text": "I’m Steve."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 22.98,
   "end_s": 24.5,
   "dur_s": 1.52,
   "text": "Nice to meet you, Steve."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 25.12,
   "end_s": 28.4,
   "dur_s": 3.28,
   "text": "Nice to meet you, too, Camila. Where are you from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 28.4,
   "end_s": 33.44,
   "dur_s": 5.04,
   "text": "I’m from Spain. I’m from a small town called Teruel."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 34.06,
   "end_s": 36.34,
   "dur_s": 2.28,
   "text": "Spain is a beautiful country."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 36.96,
   "end_s": 40.76,
   "dur_s": 3.8,
   "text": "Yes, it is. Who’s your favourite singer?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 43.36,
   "end_s": 47.48,
   "dur_s": 4.12,
   "text": "Umm … er … well, it’s that British guy, Shawn Mendes."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 48.16,
   "end_s": 49.38,
   "dur_s": 1.22,
   "text": "Shawn Mendes?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 49.94,
   "end_s": 51.6,
   "dur_s": 1.66,
   "text": "Yes, he’s great."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 52.14,
   "end_s": 56.64,
   "dur_s": 4.5,
   "text": "Yes, he is. But he isn’t a British singer."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 57.18,
   "end_s": 57.56,
   "dur_s": 0.38,
   "text": "No?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 57.56,
   "end_s": 60.56,
   "dur_s": 3.0,
   "text": "No! He’s from Canada!"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 61.32,
   "end_s": 61.74,
   "dur_s": 0.42,
   "text": "Oh!"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 62.5,
   "end_s": 65.36,
   "dur_s": 2.86,
   "text": "I need to go now. Bye, Steve."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 66.12,
   "end_s": 67.78,
   "dur_s": 1.66,
   "text": "Oh, OK! Bye!"
  }
 ],
 "p018": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.44,
   "end_s": 10.1,
   "dur_s": 0.66,
   "text": "Hi, Tom."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 10.54,
   "end_s": 12.66,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "Hi, Mark. How's it going?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 13.34,
   "end_s": 15.78,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "Great, thanks. Nice skateboard."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 16.48,
   "end_s": 18.1,
   "dur_s": 1.62,
   "text": "Oh, right. Thanks."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 19.96,
   "end_s": 21.08,
   "dur_s": 1.12,
   "text": "Who's that?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 21.74,
   "end_s": 22.98,
   "dur_s": 1.24,
   "text": "That's Daniela."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 23.6,
   "end_s": 24.44,
   "dur_s": 0.84,
   "text": "Who's she?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 25.04,
   "end_s": 27.7,
   "dur_s": 2.66,
   "text": "She's new. She's in another class."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 30.0,
   "end_s": 31.1,
   "dur_s": 1.1,
   "text": "Where's she from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 31.88,
   "end_s": 37.78,
   "dur_s": 5.9,
   "text": "I'm not sure, but I think she's Spanish. From Madrid, I think."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 38.34,
   "end_s": 43.22,
   "dur_s": 4.88,
   "text": "Spanish? Wow. That's awesome. I know."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 45.02,
   "end_s": 51.68,
   "dur_s": 6.66,
   "text": "Hi, you two. I'm Daniela. I'm new here. I'm from Manchester."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 52.62,
   "end_s": 55.44,
   "dur_s": 2.82,
   "text": "Manchester? But Tom..."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 55.44,
   "end_s": 58.88,
   "dur_s": 3.44,
   "text": "Okay. Time to go. See you later, Mark."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 59.6,
   "end_s": 60.62,
   "dur_s": 1.02,
   "text": "Bye, Daniela."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 60.9,
   "end_s": 63.16,
   "dur_s": 2.26,
   "text": "Bye. Is there a problem?"
  }
 ],
 "p020": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.68,
   "end_s": 13.32,
   "dur_s": 2.64,
   "text": "Hi there, I’m at a party."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 14.16,
   "end_s": 17.009,
   "dur_s": 2.849,
   "text": "There are lots of girls and boys here."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 17.76,
   "end_s": 19.38,
   "dur_s": 1.62,
   "text": "The food is great."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.32,
   "end_s": 21.36,
   "dur_s": 1.04,
   "text": "Lots of balloons."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 22.28,
   "end_s": 24.04,
   "dur_s": 1.76,
   "text": "There is only one problem."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 24.84,
   "end_s": 26.52,
   "dur_s": 1.68,
   "text": "My friends aren’t here!"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 27.24,
   "end_s": 28.24,
   "dur_s": 1.0,
   "text": "I’m sad."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 34.22,
   "end_s": 38.98,
   "dur_s": 4.76,
   "text": "I’m at the computer shop with Dad to get my new phone!"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 39.68,
   "end_s": 41.14,
   "dur_s": 1.46,
   "text": "Dad is angry."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 42.04,
   "end_s": 47.125,
   "dur_s": 5.085,
   "text": "The sales assistant isn’t here, but the wait isn’t a problem for me."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 47.68,
   "end_s": 48.878,
   "dur_s": 1.198,
   "text": "I’m not bored."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 49.5,
   "end_s": 51.955,
   "dur_s": 2.455,
   "text": "There are lots of cool things here!"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 57.66,
   "end_s": 61.5,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "I’m at the cinema and I’m so excited!"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 62.36,
   "end_s": 66.02,
   "dur_s": 3.66,
   "text": "It’s the first day of the new Star Wars film."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 67.04,
   "end_s": 68.72,
   "dur_s": 1.68,
   "text": "Lots of people are here."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 69.84,
   "end_s": 72.423,
   "dur_s": 2.583,
   "text": "Kim and Olivia are with me."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 73.24,
   "end_s": 75.64,
   "dur_s": 2.4,
   "text": "We’re hungry and thirsty."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 83.62,
   "end_s": 85.4,
   "dur_s": 1.78,
   "text": "We’re at the station."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 86.42,
   "end_s": 88.86,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "The train to the airport isn’t here."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 89.58,
   "end_s": 90.2,
   "dur_s": 0.62,
   "text": "It’s late."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 91.2,
   "end_s": 95.88,
   "dur_s": 4.68,
   "text": "The plane is at nine tonight and Mum and Dad are a bit worried."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 96.74,
   "end_s": 97.82,
   "dur_s": 1.08,
   "text": "I’m not worried."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 98.5,
   "end_s": 99.54,
   "dur_s": 1.04,
   "text": "I’m on holiday."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 100.4,
   "end_s": 102.56,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "No school for six weeks!!!!!"
  }
 ],
 "p023": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 12.22,
   "end_s": 15.42,
   "dur_s": 3.2,
   "text": "Why don't you go to bed, Liam?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 16.06,
   "end_s": 19.42,
   "dur_s": 3.36,
   "text": "I'm not tired. There's nothing to do here."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.86,
   "end_s": 22.86,
   "dur_s": 3.0,
   "text": "Well, go somewhere. Go to the cinema."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.62,
   "end_s": 25.46,
   "dur_s": 1.84,
   "text": "There's nothing good on."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 26.04,
   "end_s": 27.1,
   "dur_s": 1.06,
   "text": "Read a book."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 27.1,
   "end_s": 32.38,
   "dur_s": 5.28,
   "text": "Look. It's okay, Mum. Don't worry."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 36.9,
   "end_s": 38.08,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "Sandwich, Lucy?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 38.9,
   "end_s": 41.66,
   "dur_s": 2.76,
   "text": "Yes, please. Can I have two?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 42.44,
   "end_s": 43.24,
   "dur_s": 0.8,
   "text": "Of course."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 43.78,
   "end_s": 46.54,
   "dur_s": 2.76,
   "text": "And can I have that pizza, too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 47.36,
   "end_s": 51.76,
   "dur_s": 4.4,
   "text": "Okay. Two sandwiches and a pizza, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 55.76,
   "end_s": 57.84,
   "dur_s": 2.08,
   "text": "Be careful, Tim."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 59.38,
   "end_s": 65.06,
   "dur_s": 5.68,
   "text": "Tim, look! That's Mum's favourite."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 65.96,
   "end_s": 67.76,
   "dur_s": 1.8,
   "text": "Oh dear. I'm sorry."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 68.72,
   "end_s": 71.44,
   "dur_s": 2.72,
   "text": "Oh, this is really serious."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 72.4,
   "end_s": 76.26,
   "dur_s": 3.86,
   "text": "Really? Oh dear. What can I do?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 80.82,
   "end_s": 83.6,
   "dur_s": 2.78,
   "text": "Can I open the window, please, Eve?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 83.6,
   "end_s": 85.3,
   "dur_s": 1.7,
   "text": "That's a good idea."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 86.9,
   "end_s": 90.62,
   "dur_s": 3.72,
   "text": "Ah, that's a lot better."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 91.4,
   "end_s": 94.32,
   "dur_s": 2.92,
   "text": "Yes, it's a really nice day."
  }
 ],
 "p024": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.32,
   "end_s": 8.46,
   "dur_s": 2.14,
   "text": "Hi, Ben, how’s it going?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 9.0,
   "end_s": 12.58,
   "dur_s": 3.58,
   "text": "Hey! I’m fine thanks. What about you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 13.36,
   "end_s": 16.52,
   "dur_s": 3.16,
   "text": "I’m really excited. It’s my birthday."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 17.624,
   "end_s": 22.02,
   "dur_s": 4.396,
   "text": "Your birthday? Today? Isn’t it next week?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 22.64,
   "end_s": 26.58,
   "dur_s": 3.94,
   "text": "No, it’s today. So where’s my present?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 27.14,
   "end_s": 34.3,
   "dur_s": 7.16,
   "text": "Umm, err. Yes, your present. What do you want?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 35.18,
   "end_s": 37.3,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "I don’t know. A surprise?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 38.52,
   "end_s": 42.94,
   "dur_s": 4.42,
   "text": "How about tickets for the Camila Cabello concert in June?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 43.82,
   "end_s": 52.373,
   "dur_s": 8.553,
   "text": "Wow – that’s an expensive present. Camila Cabello? No, I don’t like her."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 53.74,
   "end_s": 56.56,
   "dur_s": 2.82,
   "text": "What about a book about football?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 57.5,
   "end_s": 63.4,
   "dur_s": 5.9,
   "text": "Football? Sorry, I don’t like it. I only like tennis."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 64.32,
   "end_s": 69.84,
   "dur_s": 5.52,
   "text": "OK, I know. A 5 Seconds of Summer T-shirt."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 71.0,
   "end_s": 74.3,
   "dur_s": 3.3,
   "text": "No, thanks. I don’t like them any more."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 75.04,
   "end_s": 82.86,
   "dur_s": 7.82,
   "text": "Oh. Can I take you for an ice cream in town? There’s a great new Italian ice cream shop."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 83.28,
   "end_s": 86.68,
   "dur_s": 3.4,
   "text": "Sorry. I don’t like ice cream."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 87.28,
   "end_s": 103.94,
   "dur_s": 16.66,
   "text": "This is difficult. No concert, no book, no T-shirt, no ice cream. How about a big bar of chocolate? No? You don’t like chocolate?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 104.8,
   "end_s": 107.26,
   "dur_s": 2.46,
   "text": "Of course I like chocolate."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 107.82,
   "end_s": 108.94,
   "dur_s": 1.12,
   "text": "You do?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 109.8,
   "end_s": 114.78,
   "dur_s": 4.98,
   "text": "But not milk chocolate. I only like white chocolate."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 115.46,
   "end_s": 118.78,
   "dur_s": 3.32,
   "text": "Only white chocolate. OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 120.12,
   "end_s": 124.86,
   "dur_s": 4.74,
   "text": ". I’m only joking. I don’t need a present."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 125.82,
   "end_s": 126.36,
   "dur_s": 0.54,
   "text": "Really?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 127.14,
   "end_s": 130.75,
   "dur_s": 3.61,
   "text": "Yes, and one more thing …"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 130.94,
   "end_s": 131.94,
   "dur_s": 1.0,
   "text": "What’s that?"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 132.5,
   "end_s": 136.94,
   "dur_s": 4.44,
   "text": "It isn’t my birthday today. It’s next week."
  }
 ],
 "p027": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 11.18,
   "end_s": 13.34,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "This mask is from Mexico."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 14.34,
   "end_s": 20.38,
   "dur_s": 6.04,
   "text": "People wear them for the Day of the Dead Festival on 1st and 2nd November."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 21.8,
   "end_s": 26.38,
   "dur_s": 4.58,
   "text": "This festival is popular in many countries in Latin America."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 27.4,
   "end_s": 32.38,
   "dur_s": 4.98,
   "text": "People remember family members and friends who are not alive."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 35.78,
   "end_s": 38.76,
   "dur_s": 2.98,
   "text": "This is a lion mask from China."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 40.24,
   "end_s": 44.04,
   "dur_s": 3.8,
   "text": "In many countries in Asia, there are lion dances."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 44.88,
   "end_s": 51.52,
   "dur_s": 6.64,
   "text": "There are always two people in a lion – the mask is on the head of one dancer."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 52.42,
   "end_s": 55.12,
   "dur_s": 2.7,
   "text": "The lion dances are very beautiful."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 56.0,
   "end_s": 57.88,
   "dur_s": 1.88,
   "text": "Tourists love them."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 61.7,
   "end_s": 66.88,
   "dur_s": 5.18,
   "text": "Masks are an important part of the carnival in Venice, Italy."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 67.96,
   "end_s": 71.32,
   "dur_s": 3.36,
   "text": "There are many different types of carnival masks."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 72.26,
   "end_s": 78.16,
   "dur_s": 5.9,
   "text": "For example, the mask in this picture is called the Colombina."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 79.12,
   "end_s": 85.4,
   "dur_s": 6.28,
   "text": "Carnival masks are often very beautiful and some are very expensive."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 89.38,
   "end_s": 91.98,
   "dur_s": 2.6,
   "text": "This mask is from North America."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 93.22,
   "end_s": 97.28,
   "dur_s": 4.06,
   "text": "It’s a mask from the First Nations people in Canada."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 98.44,
   "end_s": 101.14,
   "dur_s": 2.7,
   "text": "The mask is for the medicine man."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 105.24,
   "end_s": 107.44,
   "dur_s": 2.2,
   "text": "These are Halloween masks."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 108.4,
   "end_s": 111.74,
   "dur_s": 3.34,
   "text": "Halloween is on 31st October."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 113.04,
   "end_s": 121.88,
   "dur_s": 8.84,
   "text": "Children in many countries around the world, for example the US and the UK, wear Halloween masks."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 122.78,
   "end_s": 127.1,
   "dur_s": 4.32,
   "text": "They go from house to house and say ‘Trick or treat’."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 127.1,
   "end_s": 130.74,
   "dur_s": 3.64,
   "text": "People give them sweets (‘treats’)."
  }
 ],
 "p030": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.48,
   "end_s": 15.44,
   "dur_s": 4.96,
   "text": "Emma Watson is a famous English actress."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 16.6,
   "end_s": 20.5,
   "dur_s": 3.9,
   "text": "She is Hermione Granger in the Harry Potter films."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 22.18,
   "end_s": 24.8,
   "dur_s": 2.62,
   "text": "Emma’s mother and father are lawyers."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 25.8,
   "end_s": 32.56,
   "dur_s": 6.76,
   "text": "Her mother’s name is Jacqueline Luesby and her father’s name is Chris Watson."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 33.56,
   "end_s": 36.2,
   "dur_s": 2.64,
   "text": "They live in Oxford, in England."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 37.7,
   "end_s": 39.6,
   "dur_s": 1.9,
   "text": "She’s got two sisters."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 40.48,
   "end_s": 41.5,
   "dur_s": 1.02,
   "text": "They’re twins."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 42.84,
   "end_s": 45.26,
   "dur_s": 2.42,
   "text": "They’re called Lucy and Nina."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 46.44,
   "end_s": 51.62,
   "dur_s": 5.18,
   "text": "She’s also got a brother called Toby and a brother called Alex."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 52.62,
   "end_s": 54.68,
   "dur_s": 2.06,
   "text": "Emma is very busy."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 55.9,
   "end_s": 61.9,
   "dur_s": 6.0,
   "text": "She’s in many films and she is also a UN Goodwill Ambassador."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 65.4,
   "end_s": 73.166,
   "dur_s": 7.766,
   "text": "Chris Hemsworth is a famous Australian actor."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 73.88,
   "end_s": 82.76,
   "dur_s": 8.88,
   "text": "He was born in Melbourne, in 1983, but his grandfather is Dutch and his grandmother is Irish."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 84.06,
   "end_s": 86.831,
   "dur_s": 2.771,
   "text": "His wife’s name is Elsa Pataky."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 87.64,
   "end_s": 89.92,
   "dur_s": 2.28,
   "text": "She is a famous Spanish actress."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 91.14,
   "end_s": 96.08,
   "dur_s": 4.94,
   "text": "They have got three children – two sons and a daughter."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 97.24,
   "end_s": 99.02,
   "dur_s": 1.78,
   "text": "The two boys are twins."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 100.54,
   "end_s": 103.06,
   "dur_s": 2.52,
   "text": "Their names are Sasha and Tristan."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 103.06,
   "end_s": 106.86,
   "dur_s": 3.8,
   "text": "Their daughter’s name is India Rose."
  }
 ],
 "p033": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.64,
   "end_s": 11.26,
   "dur_s": 2.62,
   "text": "Tell us about your family, Ina."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.86,
   "end_s": 15.34,
   "dur_s": 3.48,
   "text": "Well, there's my mother and father."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 16.8,
   "end_s": 19.4,
   "dur_s": 2.6,
   "text": "And have you got any brothers or sisters?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.12,
   "end_s": 28.3,
   "dur_s": 8.18,
   "text": "I've got two brothers and I've also got three cousins, two girls and a boy."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 29.06,
   "end_s": 31.36,
   "dur_s": 2.3,
   "text": "My cousins are in the US."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 32.58,
   "end_s": 34.28,
   "dur_s": 1.7,
   "text": "Do you like your brothers?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 34.88,
   "end_s": 37.28,
   "dur_s": 2.4,
   "text": "Yes, they're very good to me."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 41.54,
   "end_s": 44.42,
   "dur_s": 2.88,
   "text": "Have you got a big family, Jake?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 45.08,
   "end_s": 48.52,
   "dur_s": 3.44,
   "text": "Yes, I have. I've got ten brothers."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 49.18,
   "end_s": 54.02,
   "dur_s": 4.84,
   "text": "Ten brothers? Wow! That is a big family."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 54.48,
   "end_s": 56.72,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "I've got four cousins too."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 57.28,
   "end_s": 60.02,
   "dur_s": 2.74,
   "text": "And are they all boys too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 60.64,
   "end_s": 65.34,
   "dur_s": 4.7,
   "text": "No, there are three girls and one boy, George."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 66.32,
   "end_s": 69.38,
   "dur_s": 3.06,
   "text": "My cousin George is my best friend."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 69.88,
   "end_s": 73.86,
   "dur_s": 3.98,
   "text": "I love football and he's a football fan too."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 74.88,
   "end_s": 77.24,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "Do your brothers like football?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 77.8,
   "end_s": 81.6,
   "dur_s": 3.8,
   "text": "No, they don't. They all like basketball."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 86.1,
   "end_s": 86.98,
   "dur_s": 0.88,
   "text": "Tell us about your family."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 86.98,
   "end_s": 90.34,
   "dur_s": 3.36,
   "text": "So, Maria, tell us about your family."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 91.1,
   "end_s": 95.3,
   "dur_s": 4.2,
   "text": "I've got a small family. I've got one sister."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 96.0,
   "end_s": 99.62,
   "dur_s": 3.62,
   "text": "She's called Antonia and there's my grandmother."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 100.6,
   "end_s": 102.52,
   "dur_s": 1.92,
   "text": "Is your grandmother nice?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 103.46,
   "end_s": 109.26,
   "dur_s": 5.8,
   "text": "Oh yes, she's great. She's very kind and very patient."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 109.8,
   "end_s": 110.86,
   "dur_s": 1.06,
   "text": "We love her."
  }
 ],
 "p034": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.31,
   "end_s": 11.8,
   "dur_s": 2.49,
   "text": "So, is this your bedroom?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 12.72,
   "end_s": 18.8,
   "dur_s": 6.08,
   "text": "No, it isn’t! It’s my sister Ellie’s bedroom. Do you like it?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.52,
   "end_s": 29.118,
   "dur_s": 9.598,
   "text": "I love armchair here. And cushions on the chair are great! But why are we in here?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 29.733,
   "end_s": 35.991,
   "dur_s": 6.258,
   "text": "My cat, Lucky. Look! She’s on the bed. She’s always there."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 36.5,
   "end_s": 42.992,
   "dur_s": 6.492,
   "text": "Oh, yes. She’s very beautiful. Can we take her to your room?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 43.46,
   "end_s": 52.96,
   "dur_s": 9.5,
   "text": "No, let’s leave her here. She’s happy here. Come on. Let’s go to my room and watch a film."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 53.56,
   "end_s": 61.161,
   "dur_s": 7.601,
   "text": "Oh, just a minute, Anna. ’s a nice photograph. Over there, next to the bed."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 61.88,
   "end_s": 68.44,
   "dur_s": 6.56,
   "text": "Yes, it’s me and my family, on holiday in Turkey. We’re all very happy!"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 69.42,
   "end_s": 74.3,
   "dur_s": 4.88,
   "text": "Cool. And is your sister Ellie, there?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 74.88,
   "end_s": 77.46,
   "dur_s": 2.58,
   "text": "Yes, it is. That’s Ellie."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 78.42,
   "end_s": 84.12,
   "dur_s": 5.7,
   "text": "Oh, she’s beautiful. And are two people your parents?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 84.96,
   "end_s": 86.28,
   "dur_s": 1.32,
   "text": "Yes, they are."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 87.18,
   "end_s": 92.18,
   "dur_s": 5.0,
   "text": "And who is tall boy next to you? Is it your brother?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 92.88,
   "end_s": 104.32,
   "dur_s": 11.44,
   "text": "No, it isn’t. That’s my cousin. His name’s Max. He lives in Turkey with his mother and father. They’re English teachers."
  }
 ],
 "p036": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 3.24,
   "end_s": 4.3,
   "dur_s": 1.06,
   "text": "Developing Speaking"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 7.66,
   "end_s": 11.18,
   "dur_s": 3.52,
   "text": "Wow, what a cool photo! Thank you!"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 11.72,
   "end_s": 13.28,
   "dur_s": 1.56,
   "text": "Who are all those people?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 13.74,
   "end_s": 18.14,
   "dur_s": 4.4,
   "text": "That's my family of course, on holiday in Spain."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 19.0,
   "end_s": 20.18,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "Ah, okay."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 20.98,
   "end_s": 26.34,
   "dur_s": 5.36,
   "text": "So, those are your parents and that's your brother?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 26.96,
   "end_s": 29.06,
   "dur_s": 2.1,
   "text": "No, that's my cousin."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 29.8,
   "end_s": 33.86,
   "dur_s": 4.06,
   "text": "My brother is this one here. Really?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 34.76,
   "end_s": 38.74,
   "dur_s": 3.98,
   "text": "Your cousin looks like your brother. I know."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 39.44,
   "end_s": 40.46,
   "dur_s": 1.02,
   "text": "Excuse me?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 41.26,
   "end_s": 42.14,
   "dur_s": 0.88,
   "text": "Hello everyone."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 43.08,
   "end_s": 43.98,
   "dur_s": 0.9,
   "text": "Oh, hello."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 44.66,
   "end_s": 48.32,
   "dur_s": 3.66,
   "text": "Abby, it's almost dinner time. Oh, right."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 49.12,
   "end_s": 50.1,
   "dur_s": 0.98,
   "text": "Just a minute, Mum."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 50.54,
   "end_s": 53.54,
   "dur_s": 3.0,
   "text": "Come on, Paul. Let's go. Sorry."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 53.54,
   "end_s": 57.86,
   "dur_s": 4.32,
   "text": "Let's look at more photos tomorrow. Sure."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 58.48,
   "end_s": 61.02,
   "dur_s": 2.54,
   "text": "That sounds great. See you, Abby."
  }
 ],
 "p038": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.8,
   "end_s": 16.16,
   "dur_s": 7.36,
   "text": "Istanbul, Turkey The wonderful city of Istanbul is a great place to visit."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 17.26,
   "end_s": 22.5,
   "dur_s": 5.24,
   "text": "It is an old city, but there are some modern things to see, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 23.46,
   "end_s": 31.12,
   "dur_s": 7.66,
   "text": "You can visit the beautiful Topkapi Palace and then go to Sultanahmet Square."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 32.22,
   "end_s": 40.7,
   "dur_s": 8.48,
   "text": "On one side of the square is the Blue Mosque, and, on the other side, the museum of Hagia Sofia."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 42.24,
   "end_s": 49.122,
   "dur_s": 6.882,
   "text": "Take a boat trip on the Bosphorus – the water between the two sides of the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 49.94,
   "end_s": 55.7,
   "dur_s": 5.76,
   "text": "Then stop and have coffee – there are many cafés in the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 57.12,
   "end_s": 59.48,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "Are there any good places to eat?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 60.52,
   "end_s": 61.28,
   "dur_s": 0.76,
   "text": "Of course!"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 62.2,
   "end_s": 70.04,
   "dur_s": 7.84,
   "text": "There are many restaurants, and you can eat great fish for lunch or dinner at Kumkapi Market."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 71.78,
   "end_s": 82.12,
   "dur_s": 10.34,
   "text": "Nara, Japan Nara is an old city in Japan, about 400 km from Tokyo."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 83.46,
   "end_s": 93.0,
   "dur_s": 9.54,
   "text": "It isn’t very big – about 400,000 people live there – but it is famous for many things."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 94.42,
   "end_s": 101.46,
   "dur_s": 7.04,
   "text": "Many visitors go to see the Todai-ji Temple, a huge wooden building."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 102.52,
   "end_s": 104.4,
   "dur_s": 1.88,
   "text": "There is a statue inside."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 105.22,
   "end_s": 108.02,
   "dur_s": 2.8,
   "text": "It’s over 15 metres tall!"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 109.56,
   "end_s": 113.801,
   "dur_s": 4.241,
   "text": "In the city there is a park with hundreds of deer."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 114.58,
   "end_s": 120.361,
   "dur_s": 5.781,
   "text": "There aren’t any walls in the park, so the deer can walk anywhere in the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 121.22,
   "end_s": 126.06,
   "dur_s": 4.84,
   "text": "Buy some special food and give it to them – they love it!"
  }
 ],
 "p041": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.16,
   "end_s": 11.22,
   "dur_s": 2.06,
   "text": "Excuse me? Yes?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.94,
   "end_s": 15.98,
   "dur_s": 4.04,
   "text": "Where's the... Please? OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 16.6,
   "end_s": 20.14,
   "dur_s": 3.54,
   "text": "Go down this street and turn right."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.72,
   "end_s": 23.44,
   "dur_s": 2.72,
   "text": "That's East Street. OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 24.26,
   "end_s": 28.74,
   "dur_s": 4.48,
   "text": "It's in East Street next to the park. Great."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 28.74,
   "end_s": 30.28,
   "dur_s": 1.54,
   "text": "Thanks a lot."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 36.12,
   "end_s": 37.64,
   "dur_s": 1.52,
   "text": "Excuse me?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 38.3,
   "end_s": 39.8,
   "dur_s": 1.5,
   "text": "Can you help me, please?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 40.46,
   "end_s": 42.74,
   "dur_s": 2.28,
   "text": "I want to go to the..."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 43.38,
   "end_s": 44.22,
   "dur_s": 0.84,
   "text": "Of course!"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 45.02,
   "end_s": 48.26,
   "dur_s": 3.24,
   "text": "Just walk down here, down High Street."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 48.92,
   "end_s": 52.26,
   "dur_s": 3.34,
   "text": "Take the second left into Green Street."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 52.68,
   "end_s": 54.02,
   "dur_s": 1.34,
   "text": "And it's on your right."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 54.76,
   "end_s": 55.9,
   "dur_s": 1.14,
   "text": "Oh, right."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 55.9,
   "end_s": 58.1,
   "dur_s": 2.2,
   "text": "But is it far?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 58.84,
   "end_s": 59.84,
   "dur_s": 1.0,
   "text": "Can I get a bus?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 60.4,
   "end_s": 62.52,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "Oh, no. Don't take a bus."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 63.18,
   "end_s": 66.74,
   "dur_s": 3.56,
   "text": "It's very easy to walk there. Three minutes."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 67.38,
   "end_s": 71.04,
   "dur_s": 3.66,
   "text": "Oh, thank you very much. You're welcome."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 77.54,
   "end_s": 80.72,
   "dur_s": 3.18,
   "text": "Hello. Can you help me? Sure."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 81.26,
   "end_s": 83.34,
   "dur_s": 2.08,
   "text": "Is there a good..."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 83.34,
   "end_s": 84.38,
   "dur_s": 1.04,
   "text": "Near here?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 84.38,
   "end_s": 86.62,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "Yes, there is."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 87.7,
   "end_s": 92.18,
   "dur_s": 4.48,
   "text": "Go down here and turn left into Green Street."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 93.08,
   "end_s": 95.52,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "Go past the shopping centre,"
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 95.94,
   "end_s": 99.02,
   "dur_s": 3.08,
   "text": "and there's a nice place on the left."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 100.0,
   "end_s": 102.94,
   "dur_s": 2.94,
   "text": "It's only four or five minutes from here."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 103.76,
   "end_s": 106.34,
   "dur_s": 2.58,
   "text": "Brilliant. I'm really hungry."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 107.14,
   "end_s": 114.6,
   "dur_s": 7.46,
   "text": "Thanks a lot. No problem. Thank you. Sure. Hello."
  }
 ],
 "p042": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.86,
   "end_s": 10.88,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "Morning. Can I help you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.52,
   "end_s": 14.26,
   "dur_s": 2.74,
   "text": "Hello. is a ticket?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 15.3,
   "end_s": 16.86,
   "dur_s": 1.56,
   "text": "Are you over 16?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 17.52,
   "end_s": 18.66,
   "dur_s": 1.14,
   "text": "Yes, I am."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 19.38,
   "end_s": 26.1,
   "dur_s": 6.72,
   "text": "OK, the adult ticket is £15.00. But are you a student?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 26.66,
   "end_s": 30.3,
   "dur_s": 3.64,
   "text": "Yes, I am. Here’s my student card."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 31.24,
   "end_s": 36.08,
   "dur_s": 4.84,
   "text": "OK, that’s fine. So it’s £7.50, then."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 36.58,
   "end_s": 38.98,
   "dur_s": 2.4,
   "text": "Great! Here’s ten pounds."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 40.22,
   "end_s": 46.82,
   "dur_s": 6.6,
   "text": "OK. And, here’s your change – £2.50. Enjoy your visit!"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 47.28,
   "end_s": 48.78,
   "dur_s": 1.5,
   "text": "Thanks – bye!"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 55.42,
   "end_s": 58.63,
   "dur_s": 3.21,
   "text": "These are nice. I really like them."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 59.18,
   "end_s": 63.646,
   "dur_s": 4.466,
   "text": "Yes, they’re very nice. Very good for all sports."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 64.04,
   "end_s": 67.18,
   "dur_s": 3.14,
   "text": "And they’re comfortable, too. How much?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 68.4,
   "end_s": 69.92,
   "dur_s": 1.52,
   "text": "They’re £150."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 71.02,
   "end_s": 74.1,
   "dur_s": 3.08,
   "text": "Really? Wow. They’re expensive."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 74.84,
   "end_s": 83.34,
   "dur_s": 8.5,
   "text": "Perhaps, but they’re really very, very good trainers. Great for tennis, running … everything!"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 84.18,
   "end_s": 87.992,
   "dur_s": 3.812,
   "text": "Yes, you’re right. OK, I’ll them."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 88.28,
   "end_s": 91.928,
   "dur_s": 3.648,
   "text": "OK, great. Let’s go to the desk to pay."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 98.66,
   "end_s": 101.24,
   "dur_s": 2.58,
   "text": "Hello. Do you need a bag?"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 101.854,
   "end_s": 104.56,
   "dur_s": 2.706,
   "text": "Um, yes. have one, please?"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 105.28,
   "end_s": 111.12,
   "dur_s": 5.84,
   "text": "Sure. They’re 5p each. Wow – that’s a lot of potatoes!"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 111.82,
   "end_s": 115.22,
   "dur_s": 3.4,
   "text": "Yes. It’s potato salad for dinner tonight!"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 116.1,
   "end_s": 119.74,
   "dur_s": 3.64,
   "text": "Oh, right! So, is that everything?"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 120.34,
   "end_s": 121.02,
   "dur_s": 0.68,
   "text": "Yes, thanks."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 121.62,
   "end_s": 128.464,
   "dur_s": 6.844,
   "text": "OK, that’s £6.95 then. How do you want to pay?"
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 128.74,
   "end_s": 129.92,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "By card, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 130.6,
   "end_s": 138.66,
   "dur_s": 8.06,
   "text": "Sure. Put it in the machine, please. Thank you. OK, bye – have."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 139.92,
   "end_s": 141.28,
   "dur_s": 1.36,
   "text": "You, too. Bye!"
  }
 ],
 "p045": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 13.88,
   "end_s": 18.53,
   "dur_s": 4.65,
   "text": "Villa Borghese is a big public park."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 19.26,
   "end_s": 24.1,
   "dur_s": 4.84,
   "text": "There are beautiful gardens, trees and some fountains, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 25.12,
   "end_s": 32.32,
   "dur_s": 7.2,
   "text": "People also call it ‘the park of museums’ because there are many interesting museums there."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 40.24,
   "end_s": 48.78,
   "dur_s": 8.54,
   "text": "Everyone knows the Golden Gate Bridge, but did you know that there is a Golden Gate Park in San Francisco, too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 49.86,
   "end_s": 59.815,
   "dur_s": 9.955,
   "text": "It’s very big (4.8km long, almost 1km wide) and at one end you can see the sea."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 64.82,
   "end_s": 73.387,
   "dur_s": 8.567,
   "text": "Chapultepec Park is an important green space in this big city."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 74.02,
   "end_s": 77.58,
   "dur_s": 3.56,
   "text": "It has a lake and a hill with a castle on it."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 78.6,
   "end_s": 81.49,
   "dur_s": 2.89,
   "text": "People in Mexico City love going there."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 89.78,
   "end_s": 94.575,
   "dur_s": 4.795,
   "text": "In Madrid there is a very big park called Buen Retiro."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 95.36,
   "end_s": 107.121,
   "dur_s": 11.761,
   "text": "There are trees and paths and a lovely rose garden, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 107.74,
   "end_s": 110.92,
   "dur_s": 3.18,
   "text": "There is also a beautiful glass palace."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 110.92,
   "end_s": 122.125,
   "dur_s": 11.205,
   "text": "The park’s real name is Parque Seminario, but everyone calls it the Iguana Park because it is full of iguanas."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 122.76,
   "end_s": 125.295,
   "dur_s": 2.535,
   "text": "The iguanas are very friendly."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 126.3,
   "end_s": 128.522,
   "dur_s": 2.222,
   "text": "People go there and feed them."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 135.0,
   "end_s": 140.56,
   "dur_s": 5.56,
   "text": "On a mountain near Singapore, there is a park called Mount Faber."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 141.2,
   "end_s": 143.708,
   "dur_s": 2.508,
   "text": "You can get there by cable car."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 144.7,
   "end_s": 150.54,
   "dur_s": 5.84,
   "text": "In the park you can walk on a long path, or on an amazing bridge."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 151.4,
   "end_s": 153.52,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "You get a great view of the city."
  }
 ],
 "p048": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.21,
   "end_s": 14.88,
   "dur_s": 4.67,
   "text": "Our school has a Robotics Club and it's brilliant."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 15.67,
   "end_s": 19.307,
   "dur_s": 3.637,
   "text": "I know this because I go to it!"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 20.41,
   "end_s": 23.417,
   "dur_s": 3.007,
   "text": "So, what is a Robotics Club?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.96,
   "end_s": 31.02,
   "dur_s": 7.06,
   "text": "Easy – it's a club for building robots and I love robots."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 32.22,
   "end_s": 35.36,
   "dur_s": 3.14,
   "text": "Mr Thomas is the club leader."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 36.12,
   "end_s": 41.72,
   "dur_s": 5.6,
   "text": "He thinks of things for us to do and helps us build our robots."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 41.72,
   "end_s": 46.02,
   "dur_s": 4.3,
   "text": "He's really cool and very kind."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 46.02,
   "end_s": 49.168,
   "dur_s": 3.148,
   "text": "He never gets angry with us."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 50.12,
   "end_s": 59.86,
   "dur_s": 9.74,
   "text": "He teaches Music (not Design and Technology!), but he just loves everything to do with computers."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 61.34,
   "end_s": 70.28,
   "dur_s": 8.94,
   "text": "We often make our own robots, but we sometimes watch videos of other robots on the internet."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 70.84,
   "end_s": 77.62,
   "dur_s": 6.78,
   "text": "When our robot is ready, we use computer programs to make it do things."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 77.62,
   "end_s": 84.5,
   "dur_s": 6.88,
   "text": "Every year there is a competition for schools all over the country."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 85.62,
   "end_s": 91.64,
   "dur_s": 6.02,
   "text": "I feel really excited when we show our robots to students from other schools."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 91.64,
   "end_s": 96.12,
   "dur_s": 4.48,
   "text": "We never win, but that's not important."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 97.24,
   "end_s": 101.6,
   "dur_s": 4.36,
   "text": "The other students like watching our robot move."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 101.6,
   "end_s": 103.78,
   "dur_s": 2.18,
   "text": "It feels great."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 103.78,
   "end_s": 107.62,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "I love Robotics Club."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 107.62,
   "end_s": 111.46,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "It's a great place to meet new people."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 111.46,
   "end_s": 117.62,
   "dur_s": 6.16,
   "text": "You make so many friends and not just with people from school."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 117.62,
   "end_s": 121.18,
   "dur_s": 3.56,
   "text": "Robotics Club is for everyone."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 121.78,
   "end_s": 130.18,
   "dur_s": 8.4,
   "text": "We meet in the school hall every Monday at lunchtime and every Thursday after school."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 130.18,
   "end_s": 136.36,
   "dur_s": 6.18,
   "text": "Come and see us – we're always happy to see new people!"
  }
 ],
 "p051": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.96,
   "end_s": 14.698,
   "dur_s": 5.738,
   "text": "My favourite piece of technology is my phone. I love it."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 15.38,
   "end_s": 18.06,
   "dur_s": 2.68,
   "text": "I use it for so many things."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.58,
   "end_s": 21.7,
   "dur_s": 3.12,
   "text": "I use it to text my friends."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 22.44,
   "end_s": 24.8,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "I use it to play games."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 25.56,
   "end_s": 29.54,
   "dur_s": 3.98,
   "text": "I sometimes use it to help me with my homework."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 29.54,
   "end_s": 36.86,
   "dur_s": 7.32,
   "text": "I use it for lots of things, but I don't use it in class."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 40.58,
   "end_s": 46.74,
   "dur_s": 6.16,
   "text": "I love my virtual reality headset. It's so cool."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 47.38,
   "end_s": 50.26,
   "dur_s": 2.88,
   "text": "I feel that I'm really in the game."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 50.94,
   "end_s": 56.28,
   "dur_s": 5.34,
   "text": "I don't play games on my TV because they don't feel as real."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 57.551,
   "end_s": 62.566,
   "dur_s": 5.015,
   "text": "The headset is very easy to wear, and it never hurts my head."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 63.38,
   "end_s": 67.3,
   "dur_s": 3.92,
   "text": "The only problem is that the games are very expensive."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 72.48,
   "end_s": 78.182,
   "dur_s": 5.702,
   "text": "My tablet is brilliant. It was my birthday present this year."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 78.7,
   "end_s": 80.42,
   "dur_s": 1.72,
   "text": "What a great present."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 81.24,
   "end_s": 91.417,
   "dur_s": 10.177,
   "text": "It's very thin and it doesn't feel heavy, but it's got a big screen, so it's great for watching films and playing games."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 92.2,
   "end_s": 99.823,
   "dur_s": 7.623,
   "text": "My mum and dad always want to use it, so I have a special place to put it where they can't find it."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 104.14,
   "end_s": 109.24,
   "dur_s": 5.1,
   "text": "My favourite things are my headphones. I love music."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 109.84,
   "end_s": 112.106,
   "dur_s": 2.266,
   "text": "I listen to it all the time."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 112.92,
   "end_s": 118.44,
   "dur_s": 5.52,
   "text": "My mum often wants the radio on, but we don't like the same kind of music."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 119.62,
   "end_s": 122.48,
   "dur_s": 2.86,
   "text": "With my headphones, it's no problem."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 123.2,
   "end_s": 128.9,
   "dur_s": 5.7,
   "text": "I listen to cool music, and she listens to the old music that she likes."
  }
 ],
 "p052": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.08,
   "end_s": 17.543,
   "dur_s": 7.463,
   "text": "How many hours do you look at a TV, phone, tablet or computer every day?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 30.7,
   "end_s": 33.948,
   "dur_s": 3.248,
   "text": "Do you check your phone before school?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 44.9,
   "end_s": 49.424,
   "dur_s": 4.524,
   "text": "Do you worry when your phone or tablet has no power?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 60.04,
   "end_s": 64.58,
   "dur_s": 4.54,
   "text": "Do you watch TV before you do your homework?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 75.38,
   "end_s": 80.55,
   "dur_s": 5.17,
   "text": "Does your family ever say that you use your phone too much?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 81.86,
   "end_s": 87.731,
   "dur_s": 5.871,
   "text": "5 to 9 – No, you don't need a break! You use it well."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 88.04,
   "end_s": 88.319,
   "dur_s": 0.279,
   "text": "10 to 12 – You're not too bad, but be careful!"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 88.419,
   "end_s": 88.92,
   "dur_s": 0.501,
   "text": "13 to 15 – Yes, you do. You need a break from tech! Do something different!"
  }
 ],
 "p054": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.26,
   "end_s": 9.94,
   "dur_s": 2.68,
   "text": "Hey, Liz. What's wrong?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 10.58,
   "end_s": 12.04,
   "dur_s": 1.46,
   "text": "I've got a cold."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 12.98,
   "end_s": 18.34,
   "dur_s": 5.36,
   "text": "So? Everyone gets a cold sometimes. What's the problem?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 19.12,
   "end_s": 26.08,
   "dur_s": 6.96,
   "text": "The problem? The problem is, there's the school concert tomorrow. And I'm the singer!"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 26.8,
   "end_s": 29.14,
   "dur_s": 2.34,
   "text": "I'm sure you can still sing."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 29.68,
   "end_s": 33.34,
   "dur_s": 3.66,
   "text": "No way, Claudio! Listen to my voice!"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 34.02,
   "end_s": 40.36,
   "dur_s": 6.34,
   "text": "She's right. This really is a problem. Oh, Liz, I'm sorry."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 41.14,
   "end_s": 44.88,
   "dur_s": 3.74,
   "text": "Don't worry, Liz. We're here to help you."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 45.34,
   "end_s": 46.5,
   "dur_s": 1.16,
   "text": "How, Claudio?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 47.14,
   "end_s": 48.02,
   "dur_s": 0.88,
   "text": "I don't know!"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 48.78,
   "end_s": 56.448,
   "dur_s": 7.668,
   "text": "Just a minute. I've got an idea. Lucy, you can sing, can't you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 56.92,
   "end_s": 61.5,
   "dur_s": 4.58,
   "text": "A little, Liz. But I can't sing with a band."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 62.264,
   "end_s": 67.86,
   "dur_s": 5.596,
   "text": "Oh, come on, Lucy. You can do it. You're a great singer."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 68.56,
   "end_s": 78.56,
   "dur_s": 10,
   "text": "OK, I'll do it for you, Liz. But this is crazy! OK, what are the songs?"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 79.4,
   "end_s": 83.08,
   "dur_s": 3.68,
   "text": "I'll tell you later. You're the best, Lucy!"
  }
 ],
 "p056": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.1,
   "end_s": 10.8,
   "dur_s": 1.7,
   "text": "Julia is 11."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.68,
   "end_s": 17.8,
   "dur_s": 6.12,
   "text": "She has got curly, brown hair, brown eyes and a big smile."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.88,
   "end_s": 21.28,
   "dur_s": 2.4,
   "text": "She's got a lot of friends at school."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 22.24,
   "end_s": 24.4,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "All her classmates like her."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 25.3,
   "end_s": 32.125,
   "dur_s": 6.825,
   "text": "At lunchtime, Julia always goes to the school canteen and buys her lunch."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 33.12,
   "end_s": 36.68,
   "dur_s": 3.56,
   "text": "Her friend, Jack, doesn't buy any food."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 37.46,
   "end_s": 39.76,
   "dur_s": 2.3,
   "text": "He just drinks a glass of water."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 40.86,
   "end_s": 45.14,
   "dur_s": 4.28,
   "text": "Jack does this every day, and Julia is worried."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 46.18,
   "end_s": 50.34,
   "dur_s": 4.16,
   "text": "One day, she asks Jack, 'Are you hungry?'"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 51.12,
   "end_s": 53.232,
   "dur_s": 2.112,
   "text": "'Yes,' says Jack."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 53.74,
   "end_s": 57.783,
   "dur_s": 4.043,
   "text": "'But you don't eat at school,' says Julia."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 58.5,
   "end_s": 62.485,
   "dur_s": 3.985,
   "text": "'I haven't got any money for lunch,' says Jack."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 63.06,
   "end_s": 66.885,
   "dur_s": 3.825,
   "text": "'My dad hasn't got a job and my mum's ill."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 67.64,
   "end_s": 69.34,
   "dur_s": 1.7,
   "text": "They've got lots of problems."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 69.62,
   "end_s": 73.1,
   "dur_s": 3.48,
   "text": "But don't worry about me – I'm OK.'"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 74.88,
   "end_s": 76.997,
   "dur_s": 2.117,
   "text": "Julia thinks about this."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 77.82,
   "end_s": 80.76,
   "dur_s": 2.94,
   "text": "At home, she's got a big glass jar."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 81.5,
   "end_s": 82.98,
   "dur_s": 1.48,
   "text": "It's full of coins."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 83.9,
   "end_s": 87.249,
   "dur_s": 3.349,
   "text": "She wants to buy an electric scooter one day."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 88.6,
   "end_s": 96.16,
   "dur_s": 7.56,
   "text": "That night, Julia opens the jar, takes the coins and puts them into a bag."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 97.26,
   "end_s": 98.569,
   "dur_s": 1.309,
   "text": "Her mum sees her."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 99.26,
   "end_s": 103.26,
   "dur_s": 4,
   "text": "'Why are you doing that?' she asks."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 103.26,
   "end_s": 109.24,
   "dur_s": 5.98,
   "text": "'My friend Jack hasn't got any lunch money and I've got some money here."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 109.24,
   "end_s": 110.7,
   "dur_s": 1.46,
   "text": "This is for him.'"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 111.54,
   "end_s": 115.252,
   "dur_s": 3.712,
   "text": "'That's very kind of you,' says her mum."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 116.08,
   "end_s": 119.455,
   "dur_s": 3.375,
   "text": "She feels happy that her daughter wants to do this."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 120.36,
   "end_s": 125.22,
   "dur_s": 4.86,
   "text": "The next day, Julia and her mum go and see her teacher."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 126.5,
   "end_s": 130.84,
   "dur_s": 4.34,
   "text": "They tell her about Jack and Julia gives her the money."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 131.94,
   "end_s": 133.944,
   "dur_s": 2.004,
   "text": "'This is for Jack's lunch."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 134.44,
   "end_s": 138.182,
   "dur_s": 3.742,
   "text": "Now, he can have lunch every day,' she says."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 139.7,
   "end_s": 145.76,
   "dur_s": 6.06,
   "text": "Julia hasn't got an electric scooter, but she's got a happy friend – Jack!"
  }
 ],
 "p059": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.76,
   "end_s": 10.5,
   "dur_s": 1.74,
   "text": "Hello, can I help?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.06,
   "end_s": 17.52,
   "dur_s": 6.46,
   "text": "Yes. Have you got anything I can give to my best friend? It's a present."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.36,
   "end_s": 23.64,
   "dur_s": 5.28,
   "text": "Yes, we've got a lot of things. Is it for a girl or a boy?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 24.22,
   "end_s": 27.48,
   "dur_s": 3.26,
   "text": "It's for a girl, for my friend, Annie."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 27.48,
   "end_s": 40.04,
   "dur_s": 12.56,
   "text": "OK. I've got this lovely little yellow rose. Yellow's a happy colour. It's a lovely present for a girl. It's got a necklace with it."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 40.58,
   "end_s": 42.52,
   "dur_s": 1.94,
   "text": "Have you got any little animals?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 43.32,
   "end_s": 49.74,
   "dur_s": 6.42,
   "text": "Yes, we've got a little silver dolphin or a dog. They both show friendship."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 49.74,
   "end_s": 62.68,
   "dur_s": 12.94,
   "text": "Oh, I love the dolphin, and Annie likes dolphins, too. They're her favourite animal. But she's got a dog. It's just like this one."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 63.32,
   "end_s": 72.8,
   "dur_s": 9.48,
   "text": "Hmm. So maybe the dog or the dolphin. I've got one more to show you. It's really beautiful."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 72.8,
   "end_s": 79.5,
   "dur_s": 6.7,
   "text": "Oh, it's a heart. And it's in two pieces. That's clever."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 80.2,
   "end_s": 85.68,
   "dur_s": 5.48,
   "text": "Yes. You wear one piece and your friend, Annie, wears the other."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 86.26,
   "end_s": 95.06,
   "dur_s": 8.8,
   "text": "Oh, that's so cool. I like that idea, but I still prefer the dolphin. How much is it?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 95.78,
   "end_s": 97,
   "dur_s": 1.22,
   "text": "It's £15."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 97.62,
   "end_s": 101.68,
   "dur_s": 4.06,
   "text": "That's OK. Can I have the dolphin, then?"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 102.156,
   "end_s": 105.68,
   "dur_s": 3.524,
   "text": "Of course. And do you want the necklace too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 106.46,
   "end_s": 112.08,
   "dur_s": 5.62,
   "text": "No. Annie's got a nice silver necklace. She doesn't need another one."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 112.72,
   "end_s": 119.176,
   "dur_s": 6.456,
   "text": "OK, then. That's £15. I've got a little bag you can put it in."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 119.6,
   "end_s": 122.241,
   "dur_s": 2.641,
   "text": "Oh, that's great. Thank you."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 122.48,
   "end_s": 123.84,
   "dur_s": 1.36,
   "text": "I hope she likes it."
  }
 ],
 "p060": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 5.64,
   "end_s": 8.754,
   "dur_s": 3.114,
   "text": "Hi, Oliver. Good to see you."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 9.125,
   "end_s": 15.08,
   "dur_s": 5.955,
   "text": "Hi, Ellie. You look happy. How's it going? How's your first day back at school?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 15.98,
   "end_s": 22.361,
   "dur_s": 6.381,
   "text": "Not too bad, thanks. We've got this great new teacher. You'd really like him."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 22.76,
   "end_s": 26.34,
   "dur_s": 3.58,
   "text": "Really? Lucky you. What does he teach?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 26.831,
   "end_s": 27.32,
   "dur_s": 0.489,
   "text": "Science."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 27.32,
   "end_s": 29.86,
   "dur_s": 2.54,
   "text": "But you don't like Science."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 30.44,
   "end_s": 42.14,
   "dur_s": 11.7,
   "text": "I do now. This new teacher's very funny. He makes us all laugh and he makes Science fun. And I understand everything. It's great."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 42.76,
   "end_s": 46.37,
   "dur_s": 3.61,
   "text": "Really? What does this new teacher look like?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 46.88,
   "end_s": 59.74,
   "dur_s": 12.86,
   "text": "Well, he's quite tall and he's slim. He's got brown eyes and he wears glasses. He's got short curly hair. It's red like yours."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 60.4,
   "end_s": 61.962,
   "dur_s": 1.562,
   "text": "He's got red hair?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 62.5,
   "end_s": 68.28,
   "dur_s": 5.78,
   "text": "Yes, like yours but your hair is straight and his is curly."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 69.18,
   "end_s": 70.46,
   "dur_s": 1.28,
   "text": "Has he got a beard?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 71.32,
   "end_s": 73.68,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "Yes, he's got a short beard."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 74.44,
   "end_s": 76.42,
   "dur_s": 1.98,
   "text": "And has he got a moustache?"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 77.06,
   "end_s": 91.72,
   "dur_s": 14.66,
   "text": "Yes … Oh, and he likes sport. He plays rugby and he likes football. He goes to football matches at the weekends with his son. His son's the same age as us."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 92.34,
   "end_s": 96.78,
   "dur_s": 4.44,
   "text": "Really? And his favourite team is Manchester City."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 97.292,
   "end_s": 100.28,
   "dur_s": 2.988,
   "text": "Yes, it is. How do you know?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 101.12,
   "end_s": 104.42,
   "dur_s": 3.3,
   "text": "Is this him walking towards us now?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 105.14,
   "end_s": 106.68,
   "dur_s": 1.54,
   "text": "Yes, it is."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 107.4,
   "end_s": 109.12,
   "dur_s": 1.72,
   "text": "That's my dad."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 109.12,
   "end_s": 112.84,
   "dur_s": 3.72,
   "text": "No way! You're kidding!"
  }
 ],
 "p063": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.98,
   "end_s": 14.048,
   "dur_s": 3.068,
   "text": "How do you say hello to someone you know?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 14.8,
   "end_s": 18.36,
   "dur_s": 3.56,
   "text": "Do you smile? Do you touch the other person?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.78,
   "end_s": 22.18,
   "dur_s": 2.4,
   "text": "Here are some ideas for travellers."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.92,
   "end_s": 27.794,
   "dur_s": 3.874,
   "text": "This is how people in different countries welcome each other."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 28.48,
   "end_s": 31.811,
   "dur_s": 3.331,
   "text": "Do you do different things in your country?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 32.82,
   "end_s": 39.01,
   "dur_s": 6.19,
   "text": "In many countries in Asia, people bow their heads when they meet each other."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 40.06,
   "end_s": 41.38,
   "dur_s": 1.32,
   "text": "This shows respect."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 42.36,
   "end_s": 51.54,
   "dur_s": 9.18,
   "text": "In India, Nepal and Bangladesh, people bring their hands together in front of their heart and say 'Namaste'."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 52.96,
   "end_s": 64.36,
   "dur_s": 11.4,
   "text": "When you greet a grandmother or grandfather or another older person in Turkey, you kiss their right hand and then place it on your forehead."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 65.46,
   "end_s": 67.82,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "They do this in the Philippines, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 69.98,
   "end_s": 74.84,
   "dur_s": 4.86,
   "text": "The Maori people in New Zealand rub noses together when they meet."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 75.92,
   "end_s": 78.12,
   "dur_s": 2.2,
   "text": "This is called the 'hongi'."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 79.8,
   "end_s": 84.962,
   "dur_s": 5.162,
   "text": "In Malaysia, you put your hand on your heart and nod your head."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 85.76,
   "end_s": 90.86,
   "dur_s": 5.1,
   "text": "Sometimes you also take the person's hands in your hands first."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 92.32,
   "end_s": 97.582,
   "dur_s": 5.262,
   "text": "In Western countries, many people shake hands when they meet."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 98.52,
   "end_s": 105.024,
   "dur_s": 6.504,
   "text": "Sometimes they just smile and say something like 'Hello!' or 'Hi!'"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 105.92,
   "end_s": 113.78,
   "dur_s": 7.86,
   "text": "In the US and in other countries, some people like using a 'fist bump' to greet another person."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 114.88,
   "end_s": 121.64,
   "dur_s": 6.76,
   "text": "Both people make a fist, push their arm forward slowly and touch each other's fists."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 123.12,
   "end_s": 128.68,
   "dur_s": 5.56,
   "text": "In many countries around the world, friends kiss each other on the cheek."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 129.84,
   "end_s": 139.86,
   "dur_s": 10.02,
   "text": "In some countries they kiss one cheek, in others they kiss both cheeks and in some they kiss cheeks three times."
  }
 ],
 "p067": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.678,
   "end_s": 16.124,
   "dur_s": 6.446,
   "text": "Nikolai Kutsenko, from Ukraine, can do amazing things with a football."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 16.258,
   "end_s": 25.023,
   "dur_s": 8.765,
   "text": "He can kick a ball well ... but he can also keep the ball in the air with his feet, legs and head."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 25.47,
   "end_s": 28.68,
   "dur_s": 3.21,
   "text": "Lots of footballers can do this."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 29.5,
   "end_s": 36.921,
   "dur_s": 7.421,
   "text": "But can they do it for 24 hours and 30 minutes without stopping?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 36.921,
   "end_s": 40.383,
   "dur_s": 3.462,
   "text": "Nikolai can and it's a world record!"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 42.379,
   "end_s": 52.621,
   "dur_s": 10.242,
   "text": "Sloan Henderson, from Utah, is a really good snowboarder – and she's only 14 months old!"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 52.845,
   "end_s": 61.086,
   "dur_s": 8.241,
   "text": "Her mother and father take her to the mountains, and they put her on a snowboard – and there she goes!"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 62.129,
   "end_s": 65.466,
   "dur_s": 3.337,
   "text": "Sloan loves to be on the board."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 65.466,
   "end_s": 70.575,
   "dur_s": 5.109,
   "text": "People are often surprised when they see her because she doesn't fall over!"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 72.01,
   "end_s": 86.668,
   "dur_s": 14.658,
   "text": "American rock-climber Maureen 'Mo' Beck was born without her left hand and only part of her left arm, but she can climb really well."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 87.995,
   "end_s": 97.144,
   "dur_s": 9.149,
   "text": "She is the winner of two climbing World Championships for disabled athletes, and five national championships."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 97.89,
   "end_s": 109.456,
   "dur_s": 11.566,
   "text": "She has her own special way of climbing, but Maureen thinks she is just the same as any other climber."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 109.456,
   "end_s": 113.921,
   "dur_s": 4.465,
   "text": "Goatee can't talk or write, but she can surf!"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 115.019,
   "end_s": 116.83,
   "dur_s": 1.811,
   "text": "Why is this special?"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 116.83,
   "end_s": 119.873,
   "dur_s": 3.043,
   "text": "Because Goatee is a goat!"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 119.883,
   "end_s": 123.764,
   "dur_s": 3.881,
   "text": "She surfs with her owner, Dana McGregor."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 124.622,
   "end_s": 132.714,
   "dur_s": 8.092,
   "text": "Dana helps Goatee to stand on the board and together they ride the waves in California."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 133.756,
   "end_s": 139.42,
   "dur_s": 5.664,
   "text": "Goatee wears a yellow life-jacket because she can't swim very well!"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 139.488,
   "end_s": 146.452,
   "dur_s": 6.964,
   "text": "And now there is a children's book about her, too – Dana is the author."
  }
 ],
 "p069": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.121,
   "end_s": 10.696,
   "dur_s": 2.575,
   "text": "Hi, Julia. It's me, Mike."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.48,
   "end_s": 14.053,
   "dur_s": 2.573,
   "text": "Hi, Mike. How's it going?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 14.662,
   "end_s": 17.485,
   "dur_s": 2.823,
   "text": "Do you want to go cycling later today?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 18.388,
   "end_s": 22.419,
   "dur_s": 4.031,
   "text": "Go cycling? Good idea. What time?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 22.923,
   "end_s": 26.4,
   "dur_s": 3.477,
   "text": "How about after lunch? Say, two o'clock?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 26.7,
   "end_s": 34.901,
   "dur_s": 8.201,
   "text": "Two o'clock? No, sorry, I can't. I've got a taekwondo lesson at two."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 35.404,
   "end_s": 38.7,
   "dur_s": 3.296,
   "text": "OK, how about three o'clock?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 39.2,
   "end_s": 43.566,
   "dur_s": 4.366,
   "text": "No, the lesson only finishes at half past three."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 43.92,
   "end_s": 47.8,
   "dur_s": 3.88,
   "text": "OK, so how about four o'clock?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 48.32,
   "end_s": 52.68,
   "dur_s": 4.36,
   "text": "I can't. Mum wants to give me a tennis lesson at four."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 53.24,
   "end_s": 54.96,
   "dur_s": 1.72,
   "text": "Until what time?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 55.464,
   "end_s": 59.61,
   "dur_s": 4.146,
   "text": "I'm not sure. Maybe about quarter to five?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 59.959,
   "end_s": 66.798,
   "dur_s": 6.839,
   "text": "Really? But we can't go cycling then. It gets dark at half past four."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 67.282,
   "end_s": 71.099,
   "dur_s": 3.817,
   "text": "Well, yes, you're right. Sorry."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 71.652,
   "end_s": 75.119,
   "dur_s": 3.467,
   "text": "So maybe we can go cycling before lunch?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 75.853,
   "end_s": 81.545,
   "dur_s": 5.692,
   "text": "Um, I've got a school rugby match until about half past eleven."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 81.65,
   "end_s": 83.88,
   "dur_s": 2.23,
   "text": "What time does it start?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 84.373,
   "end_s": 85.476,
   "dur_s": 1.103,
   "text": "Ten o'clock."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 85.945,
   "end_s": 88.898,
   "dur_s": 2.953,
   "text": "Julia, it's quarter to ten now."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 89.487,
   "end_s": 94.545,
   "dur_s": 5.058,
   "text": "Really? I need to go. Let's go cycling tomorrow."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 94.824,
   "end_s": 99.798,
   "dur_s": 4.974,
   "text": "OK. Call me in the morning. See you. Have a good match."
  }
 ],
 "p070": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.197,
   "end_s": 15.665,
   "dur_s": 5.468,
   "text": "It's 15th February at Greece Athena High School, New York."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 16.732,
   "end_s": 21.012,
   "dur_s": 4.28,
   "text": "Jason McElwain is an 18-year-old student."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 22.09,
   "end_s": 23.801,
   "dur_s": 1.711,
   "text": "Jason is autistic."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.801,
   "end_s": 29.937,
   "dur_s": 6.136,
   "text": "He loves basketball and he helps with the school basketball team."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 31.409,
   "end_s": 37.595,
   "dur_s": 6.186,
   "text": "Jason practises hard every day, but he never plays in the team."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 39.131,
   "end_s": 43.485,
   "dur_s": 4.354,
   "text": "Tonight is the last game of the season."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 43.485,
   "end_s": 53.838,
   "dur_s": 10.353,
   "text": "It's Jason's last chance to play a game with the team, but for 44 minutes, he sits on the bench and watches."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 55.05,
   "end_s": 57.765,
   "dur_s": 2.715,
   "text": "It's four minutes before the end."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 57.765,
   "end_s": 63.356,
   "dur_s": 5.591,
   "text": "The team is winning, so the coach tells Jason to go out and play."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 64.324,
   "end_s": 72.55,
   "dur_s": 8.226,
   "text": "The team and the crowd are very happy, because everyone knows Jason and likes him."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 72.575,
   "end_s": 76.661,
   "dur_s": 4.086,
   "text": "Jason tries to score a basket, but he misses."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 77.633,
   "end_s": 81.385,
   "dur_s": 3.752,
   "text": "But suddenly he hits a 3-point basket."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 81.89,
   "end_s": 84.997,
   "dur_s": 3.107,
   "text": "The crowd goes crazy."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 85.835,
   "end_s": 102.033,
   "dur_s": 16.198,
   "text": "Jason hits another 3-pointer, then another and another – he hits six 3-pointers (it's a record for the team) and scores twenty points altogether."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 103.145,
   "end_s": 108.175,
   "dur_s": 5.03,
   "text": "The team wins, and Jason is a real hero."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 108.175,
   "end_s": 110.813,
   "dur_s": 2.638,
   "text": "It's an amazing night for him!"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 111.886,
   "end_s": 115.925,
   "dur_s": 4.039,
   "text": "Soon Jason starts to become famous."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 115.925,
   "end_s": 120.771,
   "dur_s": 4.846,
   "text": "People in his town know who he is."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 121.05,
   "end_s": 126.13,
   "dur_s": 5.08,
   "text": "The US president comes to Jason's town to meet him."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 126.13,
   "end_s": 132.1,
   "dur_s": 5.97,
   "text": "Jason writes a book and some people want to make a film about him."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 132.11,
   "end_s": 136.774,
   "dur_s": 4.664,
   "text": "He becomes assistant coach to the high school basketball team."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 138.096,
   "end_s": 142.34,
   "dur_s": 4.244,
   "text": "Now Jason works hard to help other autistic people."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 142.34,
   "end_s": 149.306,
   "dur_s": 6.966,
   "text": "He travels across the US to help get money for autism research."
  }
 ],
 "p072": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.76,
   "end_s": 13.75,
   "dur_s": 4.99,
   "text": "Right! Have we got everything? Tennis rackets, balls …?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 13.75,
   "end_s": 24.265,
   "dur_s": 10.515,
   "text": "Yes, I think so. And we've got some food – sandwiches, fruit and stuff – and some water. So, let's go."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 24.84,
   "end_s": 29.758,
   "dur_s": 4.918,
   "text": "Just a minute! Oh, no! It's raining!"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 29.802,
   "end_s": 31.723,
   "dur_s": 1.921,
   "text": "Now what do we do?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 31.872,
   "end_s": 36.297,
   "dur_s": 4.425,
   "text": "You're right. We can't play outside in the rain."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 36.297,
   "end_s": 42.863,
   "dur_s": 6.566,
   "text": "Why don't we go to the sports centre in town? They've got an indoor court."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 42.967,
   "end_s": 49.383,
   "dur_s": 6.416,
   "text": "No, it's always very busy. I'm sure we can't play there today."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 49.383,
   "end_s": 53.923,
   "dur_s": 4.54,
   "text": "Maybe you're right. It's a bit expensive, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 54.017,
   "end_s": 61.54,
   "dur_s": 7.523,
   "text": "OK, so we can't play today. It's no big deal. We can play tomorrow, perhaps."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 62.36,
   "end_s": 66.195,
   "dur_s": 3.835,
   "text": "Yes. But I'm a bit sad now."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 66.229,
   "end_s": 72.485,
   "dur_s": 6.256,
   "text": "Me, too. But what can we do? It's raining, and that's that."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 72.67,
   "end_s": 78.961,
   "dur_s": 6.291,
   "text": "I know! How about watching some old tennis games on the internet?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 79.5,
   "end_s": 83.954,
   "dur_s": 4.454,
   "text": "Good idea. I like watching really good players."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 84.36,
   "end_s": 86.992,
   "dur_s": 2.632,
   "text": "And we can eat our food."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 87.297,
   "end_s": 89.956,
   "dur_s": 2.659,
   "text": "Let's go and switch the computer on."
  }
 ],
 "p075": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 15.68,
   "end_s": 17.56,
   "dur_s": 1.88,
   "text": "I'm leaving home."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 18.37,
   "end_s": 20.36,
   "dur_s": 1.99,
   "text": "We're on our way to the station."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 20.99,
   "end_s": 22.44,
   "dur_s": 1.45,
   "text": "I'm so excited!"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 26.82,
   "end_s": 32.36,
   "dur_s": 5.54,
   "text": "We're standing on the platform waiting for the train to Delamere Forest."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 36.7,
   "end_s": 37.94,
   "dur_s": 1.24,
   "text": "We're here!"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 38.88,
   "end_s": 48.715,
   "dur_s": 9.835,
   "text": "What a fantastic place to see my favourite singer Jess Glynne right in the middle of a beautiful forest."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 53.16,
   "end_s": 55.391,
   "dur_s": 2.231,
   "text": "I'm eating a hot dog."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 55.88,
   "end_s": 59.88,
   "dur_s": 4,
   "text": "It's very expensive, but it's not very good!"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 64.7,
   "end_s": 67.082,
   "dur_s": 2.382,
   "text": "It's getting dark now."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 67.38,
   "end_s": 69.96,
   "dur_s": 2.58,
   "text": "The stage is completely black."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 70.7,
   "end_s": 75.14,
   "dur_s": 4.44,
   "text": "A few people are talking, but most people are quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 75.98,
   "end_s": 77.58,
   "dur_s": 1.6,
   "text": "We're waiting for Jess."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 78.4,
   "end_s": 80.02,
   "dur_s": 1.62,
   "text": "And here she comes!"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 80.7,
   "end_s": 82.12,
   "dur_s": 1.42,
   "text": "Everyone is cheering!"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 82.82,
   "end_s": 84.04,
   "dur_s": 1.22,
   "text": "What a noise!"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 89,
   "end_s": 91.5,
   "dur_s": 2.5,
   "text": "Jess isn't on stage."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 92.44,
   "end_s": 94.18,
   "dur_s": 1.74,
   "text": "Is the show over?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 94.98,
   "end_s": 96.36,
   "dur_s": 1.38,
   "text": "No way!"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 96.84,
   "end_s": 99.34,
   "dur_s": 2.5,
   "text": "We're all shouting 'more'."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 100.08,
   "end_s": 101.56,
   "dur_s": 1.48,
   "text": "Why are we shouting?"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 102.24,
   "end_s": 104.6,
   "dur_s": 2.36,
   "text": "Because we want MORE!"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 105.28,
   "end_s": 106.568,
   "dur_s": 1.288,
   "text": "But don't worry."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 106.92,
   "end_s": 109.761,
   "dur_s": 2.841,
   "text": "She's walking back onto the stage."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 114.54,
   "end_s": 116.76,
   "dur_s": 2.22,
   "text": "We're on the train home."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 117.51,
   "end_s": 119.28,
   "dur_s": 1.77,
   "text": "We aren't sitting down."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 119.95,
   "end_s": 121.12,
   "dur_s": 1.17,
   "text": "I don't care."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 121.71,
   "end_s": 128.1,
   "dur_s": 6.39,
   "text": "There are so many people on the train and everybody's a Jess Glynne fan."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 128.71,
   "end_s": 131.564,
   "dur_s": 2.854,
   "text": "We're all singing 'Hold my Hand'."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 132.13,
   "end_s": 134.142,
   "dur_s": 2.012,
   "text": "It's my favourite song."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 137.84,
   "end_s": 141.99,
   "dur_s": 4.15,
   "text": "It's exactly midnight and we're back home."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 142.71,
   "end_s": 145.72,
   "dur_s": 3.01,
   "text": "I'm feeling tired but very happy."
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "start_s": 146.57,
   "end_s": 149.2,
   "dur_s": 2.63,
   "text": "I'm going straight upstairs to bed."
  }
 ],
 "p077": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.82,
   "end_s": 8.42,
   "dur_s": 1.6,
   "text": "Hello and welcome!"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 9.48,
   "end_s": 14.559,
   "dur_s": 5.079,
   "text": "Today we are talking about different music from around the world."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 15.22,
   "end_s": 19.064,
   "dur_s": 3.844,
   "text": "Is there a type of music that you really like?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 19.7,
   "end_s": 21.432,
   "dur_s": 1.732,
   "text": "Phone and tell us."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 22.16,
   "end_s": 24.92,
   "dur_s": 2.76,
   "text": "Our first caller is Liliana."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 25.87,
   "end_s": 30.08,
   "dur_s": 4.21,
   "text": "OK Liliana, what's your favourite music?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 30.76,
   "end_s": 37.18,
   "dur_s": 6.42,
   "text": "Hello! My mother is Mexican and we often go to Mexico."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 37.86,
   "end_s": 41.378,
   "dur_s": 3.518,
   "text": "I love the mariachi music I see there."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 42.06,
   "end_s": 52.94,
   "dur_s": 10.88,
   "text": "There's a group of men and sometimes women and they all stand up playing instruments like guitars, trumpets and violins."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 53.65,
   "end_s": 56.98,
   "dur_s": 3.33,
   "text": "They also wear traditional Mexican hats."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 57.7,
   "end_s": 59.64,
   "dur_s": 1.94,
   "text": "I think they look fantastic."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 60.42,
   "end_s": 62.52,
   "dur_s": 2.1,
   "text": "Yes, thanks Liliana."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 63.4,
   "end_s": 65.22,
   "dur_s": 1.82,
   "text": "And now here's Lewis."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 66.32,
   "end_s": 69.358,
   "dur_s": 3.038,
   "text": "Hi Lewis, tell us what you like."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 69.78,
   "end_s": 70.565,
   "dur_s": 0.785,
   "text": "Hi there."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 71.2,
   "end_s": 77.973,
   "dur_s": 6.773,
   "text": "Well in Indonesia there's this traditional musical performance called gamelan."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 78.54,
   "end_s": 83.5,
   "dur_s": 4.96,
   "text": "They have these orchestras with some very unusual instruments."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 84.24,
   "end_s": 92.264,
   "dur_s": 8.024,
   "text": "They make beautiful sounds and when they all play the musicians wear the same traditional clothes."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 92.58,
   "end_s": 93.3,
   "dur_s": 0.72,
   "text": "Thanks Lewis."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 94.22,
   "end_s": 96.82,
   "dur_s": 2.6,
   "text": "And now let's talk to Jen."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 97.76,
   "end_s": 100.09,
   "dur_s": 2.33,
   "text": "I love African drumming."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 100.38,
   "end_s": 106.626,
   "dur_s": 6.246,
   "text": "I go to a lot of musical festivals and there's always some African drumming."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 107.08,
   "end_s": 111.3,
   "dur_s": 4.22,
   "text": "Is there any African country you like the drumming from most?"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 111.96,
   "end_s": 125.028,
   "dur_s": 13.068,
   "text": "Well I like all African drumming but the drummers from Burundi are fantastic and they wear these really cool green, red and white clothes."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 125.34,
   "end_s": 127.88,
   "dur_s": 2.54,
   "text": "They're the colours of the Burundi flag."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 128.82,
   "end_s": 133.4,
   "dur_s": 4.58,
   "text": "Sometimes they also paint their drums in the same colours."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 133.4,
   "end_s": 136.16,
   "dur_s": 2.76,
   "text": "Okay, thank you Jen."
  }
 ],
 "p078": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.2,
   "end_s": 7.38,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "Who are you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 7.92,
   "end_s": 9.36,
   "dur_s": 1.44,
   "text": "I'm Danny Boyd."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 9.9,
   "end_s": 12.887,
   "dur_s": 2.987,
   "text": "I'm 14 years old and I'm from Luton."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 13.52,
   "end_s": 14.36,
   "dur_s": 0.84,
   "text": "What do you do?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 14.98,
   "end_s": 20.12,
   "dur_s": 5.14,
   "text": "I'm a student at school and at the weekends I work as a DJ."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 20.84,
   "end_s": 22.98,
   "dur_s": 2.14,
   "text": "Wow, that's interesting."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 23.9,
   "end_s": 25.287,
   "dur_s": 1.387,
   "text": "Can you tell us more?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 25.76,
   "end_s": 28.793,
   "dur_s": 3.033,
   "text": "I'm a DJ at a local youth club."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 29.02,
   "end_s": 34.32,
   "dur_s": 5.3,
   "text": "I play every Saturday from 6pm to 10pm."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 35.04,
   "end_s": 38.243,
   "dur_s": 3.203,
   "text": "There's usually about 100 people there."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 39.06,
   "end_s": 40.101,
   "dur_s": 1.041,
   "text": "It's great fun."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 40.86,
   "end_s": 47.404,
   "dur_s": 6.544,
   "text": "I also sometimes play for big crowds in the park and sometimes on the beach too."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 48,
   "end_s": 50.38,
   "dur_s": 2.38,
   "text": "What do you like doing in your free time?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 50.99,
   "end_s": 55.658,
   "dur_s": 4.668,
   "text": "I love listening to music and finding new songs to play."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 56.32,
   "end_s": 63.24,
   "dur_s": 6.92,
   "text": "I like watching films and playing games on my VR headset but I hate dancing."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 64.18,
   "end_s": 67.44,
   "dur_s": 3.26,
   "text": "I know that's a strange thing for a DJ to say."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 68.24,
   "end_s": 73.1,
   "dur_s": 4.86,
   "text": "I love watching other people dance but I never dance myself."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 74.42,
   "end_s": 75.92,
   "dur_s": 1.5,
   "text": "What do you like wearing?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 76.66,
   "end_s": 81.2,
   "dur_s": 4.54,
   "text": "I like wearing jeans and a white T-shirt."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 82.14,
   "end_s": 84.265,
   "dur_s": 2.125,
   "text": "I also wear a red cap."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 85.3,
   "end_s": 87.76,
   "dur_s": 2.46,
   "text": "I don't like wearing shirts and trousers."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 88.5,
   "end_s": 90.54,
   "dur_s": 2.04,
   "text": "I wear those every day at school."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 91.6,
   "end_s": 93.84,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "Thanks Danny and good luck."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 94.38,
   "end_s": 95.086,
   "dur_s": 0.706,
   "text": "Thank you."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 95.74,
   "end_s": 98.76,
   "dur_s": 3.02,
   "text": "Why don't you come to one of my shows one day?"
  }
 ],
 "p080": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 12.74,
   "end_s": 25.658,
   "dur_s": 12.918,
   "text": "The Tango is the national dance of Argentina, and every year on 11th December people in Buenos Aires celebrate the Day of the Tango."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 26.52,
   "end_s": 32.5,
   "dur_s": 5.98,
   "text": "They do the tango in dance halls, parks and squares all over the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 33.72,
   "end_s": 37.86,
   "dur_s": 4.14,
   "text": "The dance is usually performed by a man and a woman."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 39.04,
   "end_s": 42.86,
   "dur_s": 3.82,
   "text": "The man often wears smart trousers and a shirt."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 44.4,
   "end_s": 47.32,
   "dur_s": 2.92,
   "text": "The woman often wears a beautiful dress."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 48.72,
   "end_s": 51.9,
   "dur_s": 3.18,
   "text": "The dance is often very interesting to watch."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 57.64,
   "end_s": 62.56,
   "dur_s": 4.92,
   "text": "The Whirling Dervish is a dance from Turkey."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 63.48,
   "end_s": 66.52,
   "dur_s": 3.04,
   "text": "There is a group of twelve men who dance."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 67.8,
   "end_s": 71.18,
   "dur_s": 3.38,
   "text": "They wear traditional costumes with big skirts."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 72.68,
   "end_s": 78.82,
   "dur_s": 6.14,
   "text": "They often all wear white, but sometimes the skirts are different colours."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 79.82,
   "end_s": 83.06,
   "dur_s": 3.24,
   "text": "There is another group of twelve musicians."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 84.26,
   "end_s": 87.18,
   "dur_s": 2.92,
   "text": "They play traditional Turkish instruments."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 88.44,
   "end_s": 95.76,
   "dur_s": 7.32,
   "text": "As the music plays, the dancers spin around in circles, getting faster and faster."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 97.04,
   "end_s": 99.48,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "The dance is very popular with tourists."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 106.1,
   "end_s": 113.62,
   "dur_s": 7.52,
   "text": "There are lots of Irish dances, but perhaps the most famous one is the step dance."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 114.64,
   "end_s": 118.22,
   "dur_s": 3.58,
   "text": "One or more dancers perform the step dance."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 119.52,
   "end_s": 121.96,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "The dancers only move their legs."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 122.92,
   "end_s": 124.88,
   "dur_s": 1.96,
   "text": "They move them very quickly."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 126.4,
   "end_s": 129.149,
   "dur_s": 2.749,
   "text": "The top half of the body doesn't move."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 130.42,
   "end_s": 134.28,
   "dur_s": 3.86,
   "text": "Dancers usually wear traditional Irish costumes."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 135.62,
   "end_s": 140.376,
   "dur_s": 4.756,
   "text": "The music they dance to is played by an Irish folk band."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 141.4,
   "end_s": 144.76,
   "dur_s": 3.36,
   "text": "They play instruments like the fiddle and the whistle."
  }
 ],
 "p085": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.3,
   "end_s": 12.34,
   "dur_s": 4.04,
   "text": "Harry doesn't want to be a star chef when he's 20."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 12.86,
   "end_s": 15.1,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "He wants to be one now."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 15.88,
   "end_s": 20.6,
   "dur_s": 4.72,
   "text": "This is why he's on the TV programme Kitchen Kids."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 21.56,
   "end_s": 24.86,
   "dur_s": 3.3,
   "text": "The ten-year-old New Yorker likes cooking."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 25.72,
   "end_s": 32.96,
   "dur_s": 7.24,
   "text": "He can make fantastic soups and salads, excellent omelettes and the best cakes."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 33.96,
   "end_s": 36.94,
   "dur_s": 2.98,
   "text": "But there are many other children on the show, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 36.94,
   "end_s": 39.59,
   "dur_s": 2.65,
   "text": "And they are all very good."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 40.64,
   "end_s": 44.858,
   "dur_s": 4.218,
   "text": "More and more young people are interested in cooking."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 45.08,
   "end_s": 48.14,
   "dur_s": 3.06,
   "text": "Many of them learn it from their parents."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 49.18,
   "end_s": 53.96,
   "dur_s": 4.78,
   "text": "Others watch special cooking videos for children on YouTube."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 54.86,
   "end_s": 59.78,
   "dur_s": 4.92,
   "text": "In many cities, there are special cooking classes for young people."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 60.96,
   "end_s": 64.84,
   "dur_s": 3.88,
   "text": "Some of them are for children from the age of three!"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 66.4,
   "end_s": 69.82,
   "dur_s": 3.42,
   "text": "But what must you do to become a star chef?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 71.08,
   "end_s": 76.208,
   "dur_s": 5.128,
   "text": "Of course, it's important that you like cooking and are really good at it."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 77.04,
   "end_s": 78.76,
   "dur_s": 1.72,
   "text": "But there are some rules."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 79.8,
   "end_s": 84.14,
   "dur_s": 4.34,
   "text": "You must be nine years old or more to be on Kitchen Kids."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 85,
   "end_s": 89.56,
   "dur_s": 4.56,
   "text": "'We must wash our hands before we start cooking,' Harry says."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 90.38,
   "end_s": 93.42,
   "dur_s": 3.04,
   "text": "'And of course we mustn't put them in our mouths."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 94.42,
   "end_s": 95.88,
   "dur_s": 1.46,
   "text": "A chef doesn't do that!"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 95.88,
   "end_s": 99.64,
   "dur_s": 3.76,
   "text": "And we must be very careful with hot plates.'"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 100.9,
   "end_s": 101.84,
   "dur_s": 0.94,
   "text": "The show starts."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 102.96,
   "end_s": 104.26,
   "dur_s": 1.3,
   "text": "Harry is excited."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 105.34,
   "end_s": 107.48,
   "dur_s": 2.14,
   "text": "He knows he's an excellent cook."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 108.72,
   "end_s": 115.972,
   "dur_s": 7.252,
   "text": "This time he makes tomato soup, some salad, steak and carrot cake."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 116.92,
   "end_s": 122.683,
   "dur_s": 5.763,
   "text": "The experts in the studio love Harry's food, and he stays on the show."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 123.84,
   "end_s": 125.12,
   "dur_s": 1.28,
   "text": "It's 5 pm."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 125.98,
   "end_s": 127.141,
   "dur_s": 1.161,
   "text": "The show is over."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 127.9,
   "end_s": 130.6,
   "dur_s": 2.7,
   "text": "Harry is happy, and a little tired."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 131.68,
   "end_s": 132.563,
   "dur_s": 0.883,
   "text": "He goes home."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 133.3,
   "end_s": 134.92,
   "dur_s": 1.62,
   "text": "It's time to do his homework."
  }
 ],
 "p087": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.82,
   "end_s": 12.84,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "Can we make some sandwiches, Dad?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 13.52,
   "end_s": 15.54,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "Of course you can. No problem."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 16.26,
   "end_s": 17.833,
   "dur_s": 1.573,
   "text": "Would you like some help?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 18.24,
   "end_s": 20.26,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "No, we're okay, thanks."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 21.02,
   "end_s": 23.046,
   "dur_s": 2.026,
   "text": "Can we use this cheese, Dad?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 23.32,
   "end_s": 27.42,
   "dur_s": 4.1,
   "text": "No, your mum wants that for the lasagna. Use this cheese."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 27.91,
   "end_s": 28.26,
   "dur_s": 0.35,
   "text": "Okay."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 28.68,
   "end_s": 32.66,
   "dur_s": 3.98,
   "text": "We need some salad in the sandwiches. Have we got any?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 33.1,
   "end_s": 36.98,
   "dur_s": 3.88,
   "text": "There's no cucumber, but there are some tomatoes."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 37.8,
   "end_s": 41.12,
   "dur_s": 3.32,
   "text": "Let's have cheese and tomato sandwiches then."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 41.72,
   "end_s": 42.284,
   "dur_s": 0.564,
   "text": "Cool."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 42.66,
   "end_s": 44.08,
   "dur_s": 1.42,
   "text": "What are you doing, Dad?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 44.62,
   "end_s": 49.08,
   "dur_s": 4.46,
   "text": "I'm putting some peanut butter on the bread. It's tastier than butter."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 49.44,
   "end_s": 50.32,
   "dur_s": 0.88,
   "text": "Don't do that."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 50.86,
   "end_s": 51.4,
   "dur_s": 0.54,
   "text": "Too late."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 51.9,
   "end_s": 55.36,
   "dur_s": 3.46,
   "text": "The thing is, Sally is allergic to nuts."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 56,
   "end_s": 58.08,
   "dur_s": 2.08,
   "text": "Oh no. I'm sorry."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 58.723,
   "end_s": 60.74,
   "dur_s": 2.017,
   "text": "Never mind. I can eat these."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 61.34,
   "end_s": 63.054,
   "dur_s": 1.714,
   "text": "And you can make some more."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 63.28,
   "end_s": 66.94,
   "dur_s": 3.66,
   "text": "We can't make any more. We haven't got any more bread."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 67.64,
   "end_s": 70.74,
   "dur_s": 3.1,
   "text": "I know. Can we go for fish and chips, Dad?"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 71.32,
   "end_s": 73.82,
   "dur_s": 2.5,
   "text": "Hmm, okay. Yes, we can."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 74.28,
   "end_s": 74.82,
   "dur_s": 0.54,
   "text": "Great."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 75.5,
   "end_s": 77.88,
   "dur_s": 2.38,
   "text": "And can Sally and Max come too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 78.4,
   "end_s": 79.92,
   "dur_s": 1.52,
   "text": "Yes, of course they can."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 80.56,
   "end_s": 83.28,
   "dur_s": 2.72,
   "text": "But first, we must clean up this mess."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 83.8,
   "end_s": 88.6,
   "dur_s": 4.8,
   "text": "Oh, Dad. We're hungry now. Can we do that later?"
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 89.32,
   "end_s": 90.76,
   "dur_s": 1.44,
   "text": "No, we can't."
  }
 ],
 "p088": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 6.86,
   "end_s": 9.1,
   "dur_s": 2.24,
   "text": "Hello. Can I help you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 9.88,
   "end_s": 13.66,
   "dur_s": 3.78,
   "text": "Hi, yes. We'd like a table for two, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 14.4,
   "end_s": 15.42,
   "dur_s": 1.02,
   "text": "Here are the menus."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 16.486,
   "end_s": 16.96,
   "dur_s": 0.474,
   "text": "Thanks."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 17.8,
   "end_s": 19.8,
   "dur_s": 2,
   "text": "What would you like to drink?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 20.28,
   "end_s": 21.92,
   "dur_s": 1.64,
   "text": "I'd like an orange juice."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 22.64,
   "end_s": 24.66,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "And I'd like water, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 25.26,
   "end_s": 25.72,
   "dur_s": 0.46,
   "text": "Great."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 30.62,
   "end_s": 32.7,
   "dur_s": 2.08,
   "text": "Are you ready to order now?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 33.12,
   "end_s": 36.08,
   "dur_s": 2.96,
   "text": "Yes. I'd like the pizza with salad."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 36.6,
   "end_s": 37.4,
   "dur_s": 0.8,
   "text": "Any starters?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 38.26,
   "end_s": 38.9,
   "dur_s": 0.64,
   "text": "No thanks."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 39.48,
   "end_s": 45.8,
   "dur_s": 6.32,
   "text": "Would you like any extra toppings on the pizza? Onion, peppers, or tomatoes?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 46.36,
   "end_s": 47.68,
   "dur_s": 1.32,
   "text": "Some peppers, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 48.32,
   "end_s": 49.7,
   "dur_s": 1.38,
   "text": "And what would you like?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 50.24,
   "end_s": 52.12,
   "dur_s": 1.88,
   "text": "I'd like the chicken and chips."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 52.88,
   "end_s": 55.32,
   "dur_s": 2.44,
   "text": "Okay. Is that everything?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 55.32,
   "end_s": 57.48,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "Yes. Thank you."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 61.452,
   "end_s": 63.08,
   "dur_s": 1.628,
   "text": "Would you like a dessert?"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 64.06,
   "end_s": 69.04,
   "dur_s": 4.98,
   "text": "Yes, please. I'd like the fruit salad with vanilla ice cream."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 69.5,
   "end_s": 70.16,
   "dur_s": 0.66,
   "text": "Me, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 74.52,
   "end_s": 76.06,
   "dur_s": 1.54,
   "text": "How are your desserts?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 76.96,
   "end_s": 77.36,
   "dur_s": 0.4,
   "text": "Great."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 77.96,
   "end_s": 79.7,
   "dur_s": 1.74,
   "text": "Would you like any more drinks?"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 80.36,
   "end_s": 83.02,
   "dur_s": 2.66,
   "text": "No, thanks. We'd like the bill, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 83.02,
   "end_s": 83.685,
   "dur_s": 0.665,
   "text": "Of course."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 83.72,
   "end_s": 84.04,
   "dur_s": 0.32,
   "text": "Thank you."
  }
 ],
 "p090": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.44,
   "end_s": 11.38,
   "dur_s": 2.94,
   "text": "Wow! What a great smell!"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 12.14,
   "end_s": 18.24,
   "dur_s": 6.1,
   "text": "Thanks, Mum! It's lasagna. It's in the oven and it's almost ready."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.84,
   "end_s": 20.44,
   "dur_s": 1.6,
   "text": "Lasagna from the shop?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.94,
   "end_s": 23.54,
   "dur_s": 2.6,
   "text": "No, Mum. It's my lasagna."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 23.54,
   "end_s": 30.78,
   "dur_s": 7.24,
   "text": "It's got meat, pepper, mushrooms, cheese, onion, everything."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 31.74,
   "end_s": 34.82,
   "dur_s": 3.08,
   "text": "And we can eat it with a bit of salad."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 35.68,
   "end_s": 40.16,
   "dur_s": 4.48,
   "text": "Oh, right! But we? Who's coming for lunch?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 41.04,
   "end_s": 47.44,
   "dur_s": 6.4,
   "text": "Mark and Chloe. We want to study together this afternoon and have lunch together first."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 48.26,
   "end_s": 49.8,
   "dur_s": 1.54,
   "text": "That's okay, right?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 50.54,
   "end_s": 53.52,
   "dur_s": 2.98,
   "text": "Of course, Joe. But..."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 53.52,
   "end_s": 54.04,
   "dur_s": 0.52,
   "text": "But what, Mum?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 54.54,
   "end_s": 58.72,
   "dur_s": 4.18,
   "text": "Well, the thing is, I'd like a nice quiet afternoon."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 59.22,
   "end_s": 65.271,
   "dur_s": 6.051,
   "text": "Oh, don't worry, Mum. After lunch, we plan to study upstairs in my room."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 66.36,
   "end_s": 68.1,
   "dur_s": 1.74,
   "text": "Oh! It's ready!"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 68.7,
   "end_s": 73.561,
   "dur_s": 4.861,
   "text": "Be careful, Joe. It's very hot. Can I help you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 73.8,
   "end_s": 81.66,
   "dur_s": 7.86,
   "text": "It's okay, Mum. I can just... Oh, no! My lasagna! It's all over the floor!"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 82.733,
   "end_s": 83.94,
   "dur_s": 1.207,
   "text": "Now what?"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 84.54,
   "end_s": 94.06,
   "dur_s": 9.52,
   "text": "Well, first, let's clean it all up. And then, do you and your friends want to go to the new sandwich shop?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 94.32,
   "end_s": 100.64,
   "dur_s": 6.32,
   "text": "Not really. But I've got an idea, Mum. We can just have the salad."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 101.42,
   "end_s": 110.52,
   "dur_s": 9.1,
   "text": "Okay. And you and I can make some chocolate-covered bananas so your friends can have some dessert, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 110.52,
   "end_s": 113.78,
   "dur_s": 3.26,
   "text": "Thanks, Mum. You're the best!"
  }
 ],
 "p092": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.32,
   "end_s": 16.34,
   "dur_s": 6.02,
   "text": "Valentina Tereshkova was born in Russia on 6th March 1937."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 17.94,
   "end_s": 22.1,
   "dur_s": 4.16,
   "text": "Her father was a driver and her mother worked in a factory."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 24.2,
   "end_s": 27.156,
   "dur_s": 2.956,
   "text": "Valentina was a worker in a factory, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 28.02,
   "end_s": 35.6,
   "dur_s": 7.58,
   "text": "Her hobby was skydiving and it was her dream to be an astronaut and to go into space."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 36.96,
   "end_s": 43.56,
   "dur_s": 6.6,
   "text": "In 1962, there was a big competition to find new astronauts."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 44.52,
   "end_s": 48.84,
   "dur_s": 4.32,
   "text": "There were 400 people interested in going to space."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 50.06,
   "end_s": 55.72,
   "dur_s": 5.66,
   "text": "The training programme wasn't very easy, but Tereshkova was hardworking."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 56.14,
   "end_s": 59.455,
   "dur_s": 3.315,
   "text": "And she was the lucky one."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 60.894,
   "end_s": 68.185,
   "dur_s": 7.291,
   "text": "Tereshkova's big day was on 16th June 1963, and she was just 26."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 69.6,
   "end_s": 77.48,
   "dur_s": 7.88,
   "text": "The next year, she married Andrian Nikolayev, and Tereshkova was the first woman in space."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 78.58,
   "end_s": 88.38,
   "dur_s": 9.8,
   "text": "The flight was very difficult because there were many technical problems and Tereshkova wasn't very well for most of the flight."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 89.46,
   "end_s": 92.311,
   "dur_s": 2.851,
   "text": "She was in space for three days."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 93.4,
   "end_s": 97.18,
   "dur_s": 3.78,
   "text": "She is the only woman to fly into space alone."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 98.56,
   "end_s": 103.027,
   "dur_s": 4.467,
   "text": "After that, she was very famous all over the world."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 104.22,
   "end_s": 107,
   "dur_s": 2.78,
   "text": "Her face was on stamps in many countries."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 108.42,
   "end_s": 119.76,
   "dur_s": 11.34,
   "text": "In the year 2000, there was a big celebration in London, and Valentina Tereshkova was named 'Woman of the Century'."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 121.1,
   "end_s": 132.7,
   "dur_s": 11.6,
   "text": "At the opening ceremony of the Winter Olympics in Russia in 2014, Valentina Tereshkova was one of the carriers of the Olympic flag."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 132.7,
   "end_s": 136.88,
   "dur_s": 4.18,
   "text": "These were very important moments for her."
  }
 ],
 "p095": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.62,
   "end_s": 11.36,
   "dur_s": 3.74,
   "text": "Hi Will, how are you? Are you better?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.98,
   "end_s": 18.17,
   "dur_s": 6.19,
   "text": "Yes, thanks. I was ill yesterday and the day before but I'm okay now."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 18.48,
   "end_s": 20.1,
   "dur_s": 1.62,
   "text": "Good, I'm pleased."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.88,
   "end_s": 26.02,
   "dur_s": 5.14,
   "text": "So yesterday was the prize-giving at school, right? Was it good?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 26.02,
   "end_s": 33.44,
   "dur_s": 7.42,
   "text": "No, it wasn't. Well, not really. There weren't many parents there."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 33.98,
   "end_s": 39.578,
   "dur_s": 5.598,
   "text": "Oh really? There were lots last year. Were all the teachers there?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 40.1,
   "end_s": 44.2,
   "dur_s": 4.1,
   "text": "Of course! The teachers can't choose, can they?"
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 45.28,
   "end_s": 51.583,
   "dur_s": 6.303,
   "text": "No, and neither can the kids. Anyway, who were the big winners this year?"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 52.08,
   "end_s": 58.77,
   "dur_s": 6.69,
   "text": "Well, the best student of the year for the whole school was Sandra Hammond."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 59.24,
   "end_s": 63.32,
   "dur_s": 4.08,
   "text": "Sandra? Was she the best student last year too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 64.06,
   "end_s": 72.853,
   "dur_s": 8.793,
   "text": "No, she wasn't. It was her brother Tom. This year, Tom was the best sports person in the school."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 73.24,
   "end_s": 78.66,
   "dur_s": 5.42,
   "text": "Oh, the Hammonds! They always win everything! Boring!"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 79.38,
   "end_s": 88.58,
   "dur_s": 9.2,
   "text": "I know, but it's okay. They're leaving at the end of term, so next year, who knows? Maybe you!"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 89.1,
   "end_s": 92.94,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "You're joking of course. I'm never the best at anything."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 93.88,
   "end_s": 98.74,
   "dur_s": 4.86,
   "text": "Well, anyway, guess who the best science student was?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 99.44,
   "end_s": 102.47,
   "dur_s": 3.03,
   "text": "No idea. Andy Clarkson?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 102.82,
   "end_s": 104.64,
   "dur_s": 1.82,
   "text": "No, me!"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 105.3,
   "end_s": 114.96,
   "dur_s": 9.66,
   "text": "You? Really? Well done! That's fantastic! I'm proud of you. Was the prize something nice?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 115.48,
   "end_s": 121.974,
   "dur_s": 6.494,
   "text": "Yes, it was. A book about science. I really want to read it."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 122.34,
   "end_s": 126.24,
   "dur_s": 3.9,
   "text": "Good for you, Alice. Well done. Thanks, Will."
  }
 ],
 "p096": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.42,
   "end_s": 18.46,
   "dur_s": 10.04,
   "text": "Yesterday, I was online and I learned about a woman called Amy who walked all round the UK to get money for charity."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 18.46,
   "end_s": 20.34,
   "dur_s": 1.88,
   "text": "And in winter!"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 20.34,
   "end_s": 22.76,
   "dur_s": 2.42,
   "text": "When there was rain and snow!"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.8,
   "end_s": 27.64,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "Do you know any other amazing stories like that?"
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 28.6,
   "end_s": 31.1,
   "dur_s": 2.5,
   "text": "How about Dee Caffari?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 31.68,
   "end_s": 35.56,
   "dur_s": 3.88,
   "text": "She sailed around the world, non-stop, three times!"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 36.3,
   "end_s": 38.32,
   "dur_s": 2.02,
   "text": "That’s right, three times."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 38.998,
   "end_s": 41.06,
   "dur_s": 2.062,
   "text": "Imagine the wind and the rain!"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 41.68,
   "end_s": 43.119,
   "dur_s": 1.439,
   "text": "Fantastic, eh?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 45.08,
   "end_s": 55.635,
   "dur_s": 10.555,
   "text": "OK, well there’s a boy called Jordan Romero, from the US – he climbed Mount Everest when he was 13 years old."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 56.26,
   "end_s": 60.52,
   "dur_s": 4.26,
   "text": "It’s really cold up there, but he managed to get to the top."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 61.1,
   "end_s": 62.22,
   "dur_s": 1.12,
   "text": "Only 13!"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 63.04,
   "end_s": 64.96,
   "dur_s": 1.92,
   "text": "Now that’s an achievement."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 67.94,
   "end_s": 74.08,
   "dur_s": 6.14,
   "text": "My friend Corey Armstrong decided to run a marathon when he was 16."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 75,
   "end_s": 78.507,
   "dur_s": 3.507,
   "text": "He finished in just over four hours."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 79.25,
   "end_s": 87.34,
   "dur_s": 8.09,
   "text": "He enjoyed it a lot, so then he decided to do the marathon in Death Valley in the US."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 88.14,
   "end_s": 93.92,
   "dur_s": 5.78,
   "text": "It’s so hot there – often more than 40 degrees Celsius."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 95.04,
   "end_s": 102.9,
   "dur_s": 7.86,
   "text": "This time he was slower, almost five hours – but I still think it’s fantastic."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 104.24,
   "end_s": 108.32,
   "dur_s": 4.08,
   "text": "42 kilometres when it’s over 40 degrees!"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 108.36,
   "end_s": 111.38,
   "dur_s": 3.02,
   "text": "I think he almost died!"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 114.98,
   "end_s": 126.63,
   "dur_s": 11.65,
   "text": "Before 1926, a lot of women tried to swim the cold water of the English Channel from England to France – but they all failed."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 127.44,
   "end_s": 140.92,
   "dur_s": 13.48,
   "text": "But in 1926, Gertrude Ederle (an Olympic gold medal swimmer) arrived on an English beach after 14 hours and 31 minutes."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 141.68,
   "end_s": 145.7,
   "dur_s": 4.02,
   "text": "She returned to her home in New York a hero!"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 146.82,
   "end_s": 147.78,
   "dur_s": 0.96,
   "text": "How about that!?"
  }
 ],
 "p099": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.12,
   "end_s": 13.305,
   "dur_s": 4.185,
   "text": "There are many wonderful statues all over the world."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 14.12,
   "end_s": 18.4,
   "dur_s": 4.28,
   "text": "Many of them help us to remember the lives of great people."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.86,
   "end_s": 21.107,
   "dur_s": 1.247,
   "text": "Rosa Parks"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 22,
   "end_s": 36.2,
   "dur_s": 14.2,
   "text": "One day in 1965, a bus driver in Alabama in the US asked Rosa Parks to give a man her seat because he was white and she was black."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 37.2,
   "end_s": 42.028,
   "dur_s": 4.828,
   "text": "She said no and the police decided to take her away."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 43.38,
   "end_s": 49.54,
   "dur_s": 6.16,
   "text": "It was a very important moment in the history of black people's rights in the US."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 49.54,
   "end_s": 58.86,
   "dur_s": 9.32,
   "text": "The statue shows Rosa sitting on a rock wearing the same clothes as that day in 1965."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 60.76,
   "end_s": 62.18,
   "dur_s": 1.42,
   "text": "Franz Kafka"
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 63.2,
   "end_s": 66.8,
   "dur_s": 3.6,
   "text": "Franz Kafka was a writer from Prague."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 67.44,
   "end_s": 70.34,
   "dur_s": 2.9,
   "text": "He was born in 1883."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 71.2,
   "end_s": 73.32,
   "dur_s": 2.12,
   "text": "His books were in German."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 74.92,
   "end_s": 81.096,
   "dur_s": 6.176,
   "text": "In his life, he was not very famous, but now he is."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 81.96,
   "end_s": 84.56,
   "dur_s": 2.6,
   "text": "Many of his stories were very strange."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 85.8,
   "end_s": 89.32,
   "dur_s": 3.52,
   "text": "There's a very unusual statue of him in Prague."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 90.26,
   "end_s": 93.693,
   "dur_s": 3.433,
   "text": "He's sitting on the shoulders of an empty suit."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 95.66,
   "end_s": 96.92,
   "dur_s": 1.26,
   "text": "Os Candango"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 97.78,
   "end_s": 111.537,
   "dur_s": 13.757,
   "text": "The Candango were men who travelled from all over Brazil between 1956 and 1960 to build the new capital city of Brazil, Brasilia."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 112.22,
   "end_s": 124.738,
   "dur_s": 12.518,
   "text": "In 1956, 256 men arrived, but before long there were 30,000 who worked hard to build the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 125.94,
   "end_s": 136.84,
   "dur_s": 10.9,
   "text": "Brasilia opened in 1960 and this 8 meter high statue to remember the Candango is in the 3 powers square."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 138.06,
   "end_s": 141.32,
   "dur_s": 3.26,
   "text": "The two figures are holding digging tools."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 143.04,
   "end_s": 144.916,
   "dur_s": 1.876,
   "text": "Suzanne Lenglen"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 145.62,
   "end_s": 152.613,
   "dur_s": 6.993,
   "text": "At the Roland Garros tennis centre in Paris, there is a court called Suzanne Lenglen."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 153.48,
   "end_s": 160.5,
   "dur_s": 7.02,
   "text": "Lenglen was a famous French tennis player who played from 1914 to 1926."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 161.7,
   "end_s": 164.5,
   "dur_s": 2.8,
   "text": "She was the number one player for many years."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 165.64,
   "end_s": 168.12,
   "dur_s": 2.48,
   "text": "In front of the court is this statue."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 169.06,
   "end_s": 177.02,
   "dur_s": 7.96,
   "text": "Lenglen is jumping with a racket in her hand and she is wearing her famous white dress and headband."
  }
 ],
 "p102": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 9.22,
   "end_s": 13.76,
   "dur_s": 4.54,
   "text": "Everyone knows that dolphins are very intelligent animals."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 14.66,
   "end_s": 21.72,
   "dur_s": 7.06,
   "text": "But did you know that many scientists believe there is a special connection between dolphins and humans?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 22.62,
   "end_s": 27.74,
   "dur_s": 5.12,
   "text": "There are lots of stories about dolphins helping humans who are in danger."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 27.74,
   "end_s": 31.01,
   "dur_s": 3.27,
   "text": "Here are two of our favourites."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 33.44,
   "end_s": 43.514,
   "dur_s": 10.074,
   "text": "14-year-old Davide Cecchi was in his father's boat off the southeast coast of Italy when he had an accident and fell into the water."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 44.3,
   "end_s": 52.419,
   "dur_s": 8.119,
   "text": "Davide didn't know how to swim, and his father didn't see him fall, so he didn't stop the boat."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 53.1,
   "end_s": 56.181,
   "dur_s": 3.081,
   "text": "He shouted, but his dad didn't hear him."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 56.96,
   "end_s": 58.967,
   "dur_s": 2.007,
   "text": "Davide got very worried."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 59.78,
   "end_s": 63.971,
   "dur_s": 4.191,
   "text": "Then, very quickly, a dolphin came to help him."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 64.58,
   "end_s": 71.773,
   "dur_s": 7.193,
   "text": "It gave Davide a push back up to the top of the water, and the boy got on to the dolphin's back."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 72.52,
   "end_s": 75.105,
   "dur_s": 2.585,
   "text": "The dolphin took him back to the boat."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 75.98,
   "end_s": 81,
   "dur_s": 5.02,
   "text": "When Davide's father saw his son, he pulled him from the water."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 81.8,
   "end_s": 84.602,
   "dur_s": 2.802,
   "text": "The dolphin saved Davide's life."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 86.18,
   "end_s": 96.107,
   "dur_s": 9.927,
   "text": "In 2016, Adam Walker went to New Zealand to swim across the Cook Strait between the North and South Islands."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 96.92,
   "end_s": 101.506,
   "dur_s": 4.586,
   "text": "He was swimming when he saw a large dark shape below him."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 102.14,
   "end_s": 107.671,
   "dur_s": 5.531,
   "text": "He knew that it was a great white shark and his life was in danger."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 108.44,
   "end_s": 111.36,
   "dur_s": 2.92,
   "text": "Adam knew he didn't have a lot of time."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 111.36,
   "end_s": 121.26,
   "dur_s": 9.9,
   "text": "A few seconds later, a group of ten dolphins joined him and swam in a circle between him and the shark."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 122.42,
   "end_s": 125.353,
   "dur_s": 2.933,
   "text": "The circle of dolphins kept Adam safe."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 126.02,
   "end_s": 133.32,
   "dur_s": 7.3,
   "text": "After half an hour, the shark left, but the dolphins swam with him for another hour."
  }
 ],
 "p105": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.32,
   "end_s": 11.02,
   "dur_s": 3.7,
   "text": "Hey Josh, did you have a good holiday?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 11.6,
   "end_s": 14.32,
   "dur_s": 2.72,
   "text": "Hi Mandy, yes it was great."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 14.96,
   "end_s": 15.86,
   "dur_s": 0.9,
   "text": "Where did you go?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 16.52,
   "end_s": 22.732,
   "dur_s": 6.212,
   "text": "The Pantanal, it's in the east of Brazil. It's a really big wetland."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 23.2,
   "end_s": 27.06,
   "dur_s": 3.86,
   "text": "Oh right, so why did you go there?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 27.06,
   "end_s": 31.324,
   "dur_s": 4.264,
   "text": "Because there are amazing animals and birds there."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 31.777,
   "end_s": 36.42,
   "dur_s": 4.643,
   "text": "We all love animals in my family, especially my dad."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 36.8,
   "end_s": 38.243,
   "dur_s": 1.443,
   "text": "He's a bird watcher."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 38.68,
   "end_s": 41,
   "dur_s": 2.32,
   "text": "Really? I didn't know that."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 41.54,
   "end_s": 43.76,
   "dur_s": 2.22,
   "text": "Yes, he loves birds."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 44.34,
   "end_s": 47.4,
   "dur_s": 3.06,
   "text": "So are you a big bird watcher too?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 48.04,
   "end_s": 57.44,
   "dur_s": 9.4,
   "text": "Well I like them and we saw some really beautiful parrots and toucans, but I prefer the other animals."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 58.2,
   "end_s": 60.2,
   "dur_s": 2,
   "text": "Did you see anything special?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 60.92,
   "end_s": 62.88,
   "dur_s": 1.96,
   "text": "Yes, loads of stuff."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 63.56,
   "end_s": 65.12,
   "dur_s": 1.56,
   "text": "There were lots of Cayman."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 65.54,
   "end_s": 67.72,
   "dur_s": 2.18,
   "text": "Cayman? What are they?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 68.26,
   "end_s": 70.32,
   "dur_s": 2.06,
   "text": "They're like small crocodiles."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 70.76,
   "end_s": 73.607,
   "dur_s": 2.847,
   "text": "Cool, what else did you see?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 74.02,
   "end_s": 85.368,
   "dur_s": 11.348,
   "text": "We saw an anaconda, you know one of those really big snakes, and then one night we heard a jaguar but we didn't see it."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 85.7,
   "end_s": 88.2,
   "dur_s": 2.5,
   "text": "Wow, were you scared?"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 89.014,
   "end_s": 95.109,
   "dur_s": 6.095,
   "text": "No, it was exciting, especially because it was so near our tent."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 95.5,
   "end_s": 97.98,
   "dur_s": 2.48,
   "text": "Tent? Did you go camping?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 98.72,
   "end_s": 104.74,
   "dur_s": 6.02,
   "text": "Yes, but just for a few nights. Most of the time we were in small hotels."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 105.44,
   "end_s": 110.26,
   "dur_s": 4.82,
   "text": "So how did you travel around? Did you have a guide?"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 110.84,
   "end_s": 112.14,
   "dur_s": 1.3,
   "text": "Yes, we did."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 112.8,
   "end_s": 113.98,
   "dur_s": 1.18,
   "text": "His name was Sergio."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 114.92,
   "end_s": 117.02,
   "dur_s": 2.1,
   "text": "He knew where to find all the animals."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 117.76,
   "end_s": 119.1,
   "dur_s": 1.34,
   "text": "Did he speak English?"
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 119.7,
   "end_s": 128.24,
   "dur_s": 8.54,
   "text": "Yes, he did. His English was good which was lucky because no one in my family can speak Portuguese."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 129.02,
   "end_s": 131.7,
   "dur_s": 2.68,
   "text": "It sounds like you had a great time."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 132.22,
   "end_s": 134.4,
   "dur_s": 2.18,
   "text": "We did. It was fantastic."
  }
 ],
 "p106": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.28,
   "end_s": 9.84,
   "dur_s": 1.56,
   "text": "1."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 10.844,
   "end_s": 12.02,
   "dur_s": 1.176,
   "text": "The Great Auk"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 13.01,
   "end_s": 18.56,
   "dur_s": 5.55,
   "text": "The Great Auk was a large seabird that lived in the North Atlantic."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 19.52,
   "end_s": 22.4,
   "dur_s": 2.88,
   "text": "It was a bird but it couldn't fly."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 23.6,
   "end_s": 26.4,
   "dur_s": 2.8,
   "text": "It could swim underwater really well."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 27.4,
   "end_s": 31.3,
   "dur_s": 3.9,
   "text": "It caught and ate fish when it dived under the water."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 32.66,
   "end_s": 38.32,
   "dur_s": 5.66,
   "text": "Its feathers were very soft and people used them to make pillows for their beds."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 39.34,
   "end_s": 42.18,
   "dur_s": 2.84,
   "text": "Because of this people killed the birds."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 43.32,
   "end_s": 48.62,
   "dur_s": 5.3,
   "text": "The last Great Auk died on the island of Eldey in 1835."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 51,
   "end_s": 51.24,
   "dur_s": 0.24,
   "text": "2."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 52.349,
   "end_s": 53.66,
   "dur_s": 1.311,
   "text": "The Tasmanian Tiger"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 55.04,
   "end_s": 61.46,
   "dur_s": 6.42,
   "text": "The Tasmanian Tiger was only found in Australia, Tasmania and New Guinea."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 62.28,
   "end_s": 69.38,
   "dur_s": 7.1,
   "text": "It got its name because it had stripes like a tiger but it was not a member of the cat family."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 70.46,
   "end_s": 77.322,
   "dur_s": 6.862,
   "text": "Farmers believed Tasmanian Tigers killed their sheep so they paid people to kill them."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 78.36,
   "end_s": 84.74,
   "dur_s": 6.38,
   "text": "Many of the tigers died after getting ill from diseases they caught from other animals."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 86.04,
   "end_s": 91.72,
   "dur_s": 5.68,
   "text": "The last Tasmanian Tiger died in Hobart Zoo in 1936."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 93.5,
   "end_s": 94.34,
   "dur_s": 0.84,
   "text": "3."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 95.6,
   "end_s": 96.86,
   "dur_s": 1.26,
   "text": "Steller's Sea Cow"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 98.28,
   "end_s": 105.9,
   "dur_s": 7.62,
   "text": "Steller's Sea Cow was a large animal that lived in the cold Arctic waters around Alaska."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 106.7,
   "end_s": 109.923,
   "dur_s": 3.223,
   "text": "It grew up to nine metres long."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 110.74,
   "end_s": 114.8,
   "dur_s": 4.06,
   "text": "Because it was so big it couldn't go under the water."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 115.5,
   "end_s": 118.375,
   "dur_s": 2.875,
   "text": "It ate the plants on top of the sea."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 118.96,
   "end_s": 121.394,
   "dur_s": 2.434,
   "text": "It wasn't a very dangerous animal."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 121.78,
   "end_s": 123.1,
   "dur_s": 1.32,
   "text": "It was quite friendly."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 123.1,
   "end_s": 127.048,
   "dur_s": 3.948,
   "text": "Because of this it was very easy to kill."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 127.66,
   "end_s": 131.92,
   "dur_s": 4.26,
   "text": "Europeans first found the sea cow in 1741."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 132.992,
   "end_s": 136.66,
   "dur_s": 3.668,
   "text": "27 years later they killed the last one."
  }
 ],
 "p108": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.4,
   "end_s": 12.1,
   "dur_s": 4.7,
   "text": "Hey Nathan, how are you? Did you have a good weekend?"
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 12.9,
   "end_s": 16.7,
   "dur_s": 3.8,
   "text": "Well, sort of. I mean, it was okay."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 17.26,
   "end_s": 20.6,
   "dur_s": 3.34,
   "text": "You don't sound very sure. What happened?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 21.36,
   "end_s": 23.58,
   "dur_s": 2.22,
   "text": "Yeah, come on, tell us."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 23.58,
   "end_s": 33.53,
   "dur_s": 9.95,
   "text": "Alright, well on Sundays we usually go for a walk, my family and I, but yesterday I went alone."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 33.98,
   "end_s": 34.98,
   "dur_s": 1,
   "text": "Where did you go?"
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 35.56,
   "end_s": 41.32,
   "dur_s": 5.76,
   "text": "I went to the forest, you know, outside town. It's really nice there."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 41.74,
   "end_s": 45.58,
   "dur_s": 3.84,
   "text": "And I started walking when suddenly..."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 46.28,
   "end_s": 48.44,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "Yes, suddenly what?"
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 48.44,
   "end_s": 52.4,
   "dur_s": 3.96,
   "text": "Well, in front of me there was a snake."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 53.06,
   "end_s": 56.6,
   "dur_s": 3.54,
   "text": "Are there snakes in the forest? Are you sure?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 57.3,
   "end_s": 68.26,
   "dur_s": 10.96,
   "text": "Yes, I'm sure. It was on the path. I stopped. I didn't do anything. Then it just went away. I was afraid."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 69.06,
   "end_s": 72.5,
   "dur_s": 3.44,
   "text": "Poor you. I hate snakes too."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 72.5,
   "end_s": 78.704,
   "dur_s": 6.204,
   "text": "Why were you afraid? It's just a snake. A snake can't kill you."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 79.06,
   "end_s": 84.56,
   "dur_s": 5.5,
   "text": "Some snakes can. Anyway, it's okay to be afraid sometimes."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 85.34,
   "end_s": 90.86,
   "dur_s": 5.52,
   "text": "Thanks Lena. Anyway, that's why my weekend was just okay."
  }
 ],
 "p111": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 5.313,
   "end_s": 12.751,
   "dur_s": 7.438,
   "text": "A lot of big cities, like London, have got many traffic problems."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 13.235,
   "end_s": 18.862,
   "dur_s": 5.627,
   "text": "Sometimes a journey of a few kilometres can take more than an hour."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.59,
   "end_s": 23.202,
   "dur_s": 3.612,
   "text": "So what's the best way to get across London?"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 23.212,
   "end_s": 29.2,
   "dur_s": 5.988,
   "text": "For a very short journey, it's probably a good idea to walk."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 29.2,
   "end_s": 32.85,
   "dur_s": 3.65,
   "text": "But what happens when you want to go further?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 33.923,
   "end_s": 39.925,
   "dur_s": 6.002,
   "text": "The presenters of a popular TV show about cars decided to find out."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 39.925,
   "end_s": 48.046,
   "dur_s": 8.121,
   "text": "Each of the presenters chose a different type of transport to make the same 27-kilometre journey."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 48.056,
   "end_s": 51.3,
   "dur_s": 3.244,
   "text": "One presenter went by bike."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 51.3,
   "end_s": 54.152,
   "dur_s": 2.852,
   "text": "One went by car."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 54.74,
   "end_s": 64.848,
   "dur_s": 10.108,
   "text": "Another chose public transport – the underground and bus – and the last one travelled by speedboat up the River Thames."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 65.83,
   "end_s": 75.982,
   "dur_s": 10.152,
   "text": "They all started at the same time and the same place in West London, but who got to City Airport in East London first?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 75.992,
   "end_s": 79.046,
   "dur_s": 3.054,
   "text": "The results were a surprise."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 79.689,
   "end_s": 81.849,
   "dur_s": 2.16,
   "text": "The bike came first."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 82.547,
   "end_s": 85.202,
   "dur_s": 2.655,
   "text": "In second place was the speedboat."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 85.86,
   "end_s": 90.574,
   "dur_s": 4.714,
   "text": "Public transport came third and the car was last."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 91.756,
   "end_s": 94.111,
   "dur_s": 2.355,
   "text": "So the presenters had an answer."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 94.61,
   "end_s": 101.45,
   "dur_s": 6.84,
   "text": "The bike was quicker than all the other types of transport and the car was slower."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 101.45,
   "end_s": 106.872,
   "dur_s": 5.422,
   "text": "They weren't very happy with the result because they wanted the car to win."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 107.466,
   "end_s": 113.865,
   "dur_s": 6.399,
   "text": "They made a joke and said the bike wasn't a real winner because it was more dangerous."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 113.865,
   "end_s": 117.995,
   "dur_s": 4.13,
   "text": "But, of course, the bike is the real winner."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 117.995,
   "end_s": 120.905,
   "dur_s": 2.91,
   "text": "It's the best way to get about."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 120.905,
   "end_s": 127.071,
   "dur_s": 6.166,
   "text": "It's cheaper than public transport and it is healthier than going by car."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 127.41,
   "end_s": 132.868,
   "dur_s": 5.458,
   "text": "It's also better for our cities because bikes don't make the air dirty."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 133.816,
   "end_s": 143.494,
   "dur_s": 9.678,
   "text": "So next time you need to travel around, think before you and your parents get into the car – 'Can we make this journey by bike?'"
  }
 ],
 "p113": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 8.41,
   "end_s": 9.094,
   "dur_s": 0.684,
   "text": "Good morning."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 9.813,
   "end_s": 11.005,
   "dur_s": 1.192,
   "text": "How can I help you?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 11.574,
   "end_s": 12.087,
   "dur_s": 0.513,
   "text": "Hello."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 12.087,
   "end_s": 14.622,
   "dur_s": 2.535,
   "text": "I want to go to Windsor."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 14.697,
   "end_s": 17.021,
   "dur_s": 2.324,
   "text": "What time's the next train?"
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 17.041,
   "end_s": 19.351,
   "dur_s": 2.31,
   "text": "There's one in five minutes."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 19.55,
   "end_s": 20.139,
   "dur_s": 0.589,
   "text": "It's a fast train."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 20.942,
   "end_s": 24.015,
   "dur_s": 3.073,
   "text": "It only stops at Clapham Junction and Windsor."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 24.864,
   "end_s": 26.96,
   "dur_s": 2.096,
   "text": "You can catch that one."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 26.96,
   "end_s": 28.675,
   "dur_s": 1.715,
   "text": "And the one after that?"
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 28.685,
   "end_s": 32.436,
   "dur_s": 3.751,
   "text": "There's one at half past ten, but that's a slower train."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 33.225,
   "end_s": 35.59,
   "dur_s": 2.365,
   "text": "It stops at every station."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 35.59,
   "end_s": 36.971,
   "dur_s": 1.381,
   "text": "That's OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 36.971,
   "end_s": 40.912,
   "dur_s": 3.941,
   "text": "I'm not in a hurry, and I don't want to run."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 41.406,
   "end_s": 45.18,
   "dur_s": 3.774,
   "text": "What time does that one arrive in Windsor?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 45.18,
   "end_s": 47.063,
   "dur_s": 1.883,
   "text": "At half past eleven."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 47.467,
   "end_s": 48.79,
   "dur_s": 1.323,
   "text": "It takes an hour."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 48.79,
   "end_s": 51.658,
   "dur_s": 2.868,
   "text": "And how often are the trains to Windsor?"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 52.166,
   "end_s": 53.563,
   "dur_s": 1.397,
   "text": "They're every half hour."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 53.798,
   "end_s": 54.257,
   "dur_s": 0.459,
   "text": "Great!"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 54.267,
   "end_s": 57.729,
   "dur_s": 3.462,
   "text": "And how much is a ticket?"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 57.769,
   "end_s": 61.21,
   "dur_s": 3.441,
   "text": "Do you want a single or a return?"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 61.21,
   "end_s": 62.87,
   "dur_s": 1.66,
   "text": "A return, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 62.87,
   "end_s": 64.85,
   "dur_s": 1.98,
   "text": "Are you returning today?"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 64.85,
   "end_s": 66.339,
   "dur_s": 1.489,
   "text": "Yes, I am."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 66.998,
   "end_s": 71.84,
   "dur_s": 4.842,
   "text": "Then you can get an off-peak day return ticket for £12.70."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 71.84,
   "end_s": 75.219,
   "dur_s": 3.379,
   "text": "It's cheaper than the anytime day return."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 77.125,
   "end_s": 77.18,
   "dur_s": 0.055,
   "text": "That's £19.90."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 77.359,
   "end_s": 78.247,
   "dur_s": 0.888,
   "text": "Right."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 78.247,
   "end_s": 82.213,
   "dur_s": 3.966,
   "text": "I'd like the off-peak day return one then."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 82.707,
   "end_s": 83.251,
   "dur_s": 0.544,
   "text": "OK."
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "start_s": 83.45,
   "end_s": 85.66,
   "dur_s": 2.21,
   "text": "That's £12.70, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "start_s": 85.66,
   "end_s": 89.322,
   "dur_s": 3.662,
   "text": "What platform does the train leave from?"
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "start_s": 89.661,
   "end_s": 92.35,
   "dur_s": 2.689,
   "text": "It leaves from platform 15."
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "start_s": 92.35,
   "end_s": 96.296,
   "dur_s": 3.946,
   "text": "And what platform does it arrive at in Windsor?"
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "start_s": 96.88,
   "end_s": 98.865,
   "dur_s": 1.985,
   "text": "My friend wants to meet me there."
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "start_s": 99.269,
   "end_s": 100.332,
   "dur_s": 1.063,
   "text": "Platform 1."
  },
  {
   "i": 37,
   "start_s": 100.332,
   "end_s": 105.49,
   "dur_s": 5.158,
   "text": "But Windsor is a very small station, a lot smaller than Waterloo."
  },
  {
   "i": 38,
   "start_s": 105.789,
   "end_s": 108.663,
   "dur_s": 2.874,
   "text": "There are only two platforms at Windsor."
  },
  {
   "i": 39,
   "start_s": 108.733,
   "end_s": 110.499,
   "dur_s": 1.766,
   "text": "OK, then that's not a problem."
  },
  {
   "i": 40,
   "start_s": 111.342,
   "end_s": 112.864,
   "dur_s": 1.522,
   "text": "Thank you."
  },
  {
   "i": 41,
   "start_s": 113.018,
   "end_s": 114.28,
   "dur_s": 1.262,
   "text": "Have a good journey."
  }
 ],
 "p114": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.159,
   "end_s": 13.021,
   "dur_s": 5.862,
   "text": "My favourite journey. We all love going on a journey."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 13.888,
   "end_s": 18.513,
   "dur_s": 4.625,
   "text": "Here are some of your favourites. Thank you for sharing them!"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 19.82,
   "end_s": 29.154,
   "dur_s": 9.334,
   "text": "Adam. I love boats and my favourite boat journey is the one by ferry across the Danube River."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 29.618,
   "end_s": 32.325,
   "dur_s": 2.707,
   "text": "My grandma lives in Budapest."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 32.325,
   "end_s": 36.215,
   "dur_s": 3.89,
   "text": "When I visit her, we often go on it together."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 36.215,
   "end_s": 38.423,
   "dur_s": 2.208,
   "text": "It's not a long journey."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 38.782,
   "end_s": 40.588,
   "dur_s": 1.806,
   "text": "It's only ten minutes."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 41.216,
   "end_s": 45.691,
   "dur_s": 4.475,
   "text": "The ferry just takes you across the river to the other side of the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 45.691,
   "end_s": 48.27,
   "dur_s": 2.579,
   "text": "We don't get off the boat."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 48.679,
   "end_s": 50.855,
   "dur_s": 2.176,
   "text": "We just go there and back again."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 52.775,
   "end_s": 53.633,
   "dur_s": 0.858,
   "text": "Rose!"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 54.45,
   "end_s": 56.576,
   "dur_s": 2.126,
   "text": "I really love steam trains."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 57.335,
   "end_s": 59.615,
   "dur_s": 2.28,
   "text": "There's one in Scotland."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 60.004,
   "end_s": 67.981,
   "dur_s": 7.977,
   "text": "It goes from Fort William to Mallaig on the west coast, and it's called the Jacobite Steam Train."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 68.853,
   "end_s": 72.765,
   "dur_s": 3.912,
   "text": "It's the famous one you see in the Harry Potter films."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 73.124,
   "end_s": 79.968,
   "dur_s": 6.844,
   "text": "The one that takes Harry and his classmates to Hogwarts. But that's not why I like it."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 80.552,
   "end_s": 85.616,
   "dur_s": 5.064,
   "text": "I like the sound it makes and I like the view from the window."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 86.404,
   "end_s": 91.577,
   "dur_s": 5.173,
   "text": "It travels past lakes and mountains and beautiful beaches."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 93.497,
   "end_s": 97.613,
   "dur_s": 4.116,
   "text": "What's my favourite journey?"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 98.421,
   "end_s": 100.77,
   "dur_s": 2.349,
   "text": "My journey to school."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 100.77,
   "end_s": 106.987,
   "dur_s": 6.217,
   "text": "We live in a village and my school is in the next village."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 106.997,
   "end_s": 115.533,
   "dur_s": 8.536,
   "text": "Every morning, I walk across the fields and then along the river until I'm at school."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 115.97,
   "end_s": 118.655,
   "dur_s": 2.685,
   "text": "It's a really beautiful walk."
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 118.655,
   "end_s": 121.688,
   "dur_s": 3.033,
   "text": "I love looking for birds."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 121.688,
   "end_s": 124.328,
   "dur_s": 2.64,
   "text": "There are some lovely ones."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 125.001,
   "end_s": 128.922,
   "dur_s": 3.921,
   "text": "And sometimes, if I'm lucky, I see a rabbit."
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 128.922,
   "end_s": 132.235,
   "dur_s": 3.313,
   "text": "I love my walk to school."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 132.688,
   "end_s": 135.752,
   "dur_s": 3.064,
   "text": "But I love the walk home more!"
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 137.692,
   "end_s": 144.058,
   "dur_s": 6.366,
   "text": "Max. My favourite journey is a very fast bike ride."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 145.065,
   "end_s": 152.605,
   "dur_s": 7.54,
   "text": "My grandparents have a house in the mountains. There is a road down the mountain to the town."
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "start_s": 152.605,
   "end_s": 158.001,
   "dur_s": 5.396,
   "text": "It goes down very fast, and it goes through a big forest."
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "start_s": 159.123,
   "end_s": 163.06,
   "dur_s": 3.937,
   "text": "Every morning, we ride down to the town to get bread."
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "start_s": 164.112,
   "end_s": 171.326,
   "dur_s": 7.214,
   "text": "It only takes ten minutes to ride down, but it takes a lot longer to ride back up again!"
  }
 ],
 "p117": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 7.403,
   "end_s": 9.124,
   "dur_s": 1.721,
   "text": "Transport around the world."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 10.481,
   "end_s": 13.021,
   "dur_s": 2.54,
   "text": "The Amfibus, the Netherlands."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 14.342,
   "end_s": 19.221,
   "dur_s": 4.879,
   "text": "The big, blue Amfibus certainly makes a big splash!"
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 20.324,
   "end_s": 25.048,
   "dur_s": 4.724,
   "text": "It's in Rotterdam, and it takes people on tours of the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 25.058,
   "end_s": 26.674,
   "dur_s": 1.616,
   "text": "It's cool."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 26.684,
   "end_s": 31.015,
   "dur_s": 4.331,
   "text": "It can travel on land and in the water."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 31.025,
   "end_s": 38.073,
   "dur_s": 7.048,
   "text": "It is more expensive than water taxis, but it is more exciting, too."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 38.083,
   "end_s": 41.74,
   "dur_s": 3.657,
   "text": "It is slower in the water than on land."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 41.75,
   "end_s": 50.116,
   "dur_s": 8.366,
   "text": "It goes at 8 kilometres per hour in the water and 96 kilometres per hour on land."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 50.126,
   "end_s": 57.25,
   "dur_s": 7.124,
   "text": "The tour lasts for an hour, and it costs 27.50 euros."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 59.255,
   "end_s": 62.987,
   "dur_s": 3.732,
   "text": "Moving walkways and escalators, Hong Kong."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 64.364,
   "end_s": 69.602,
   "dur_s": 5.238,
   "text": "The Central-Mid-Levels Escalator is 800 metres long."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 71.033,
   "end_s": 78.17,
   "dur_s": 7.137,
   "text": "Escalators are usually inside a shopping centre or an airport, but not this one!"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 78.17,
   "end_s": 79.674,
   "dur_s": 1.504,
   "text": "It's outside."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 80.17,
   "end_s": 84.383,
   "dur_s": 4.213,
   "text": "It's a great way to travel round this city of hills."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 85.286,
   "end_s": 86.344,
   "dur_s": 1.058,
   "text": "And it's free!"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 87.616,
   "end_s": 91.248,
   "dur_s": 3.632,
   "text": "There are 14 places where you can get on and off."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 92.225,
   "end_s": 99.973,
   "dur_s": 7.748,
   "text": "The escalators travel down the hill from 6am to 10am, so people can travel to work."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 100.586,
   "end_s": 105.116,
   "dur_s": 4.53,
   "text": "They travel up the hill from 10am to midnight."
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "start_s": 106.25,
   "end_s": 108.698,
   "dur_s": 2.448,
   "text": "The urban cable car, Turkey."
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "start_s": 108.833,
   "end_s": 115.812,
   "dur_s": 6.979,
   "text": "Ankara's cable car is cheaper than other forms of public transport."
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "start_s": 115.822,
   "end_s": 119.873,
   "dur_s": 4.051,
   "text": "It is healthier because it doesn't pollute the air."
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "start_s": 119.883,
   "end_s": 128.343,
   "dur_s": 8.46,
   "text": "It is also easier and quicker than travelling by car, because there are no traffic jams in the sky!"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "start_s": 128.353,
   "end_s": 136.55,
   "dur_s": 8.197,
   "text": "It travels 60 metres above the ground, and passengers can get great views of the city."
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "start_s": 138.52,
   "end_s": 142.641,
   "dur_s": 4.121,
   "text": "Submarines, Lanzarote and Tenerife."
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "start_s": 144.087,
   "end_s": 147.051,
   "dur_s": 2.964,
   "text": "Now you can travel in a submarine!"
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "start_s": 147.061,
   "end_s": 150.897,
   "dur_s": 3.836,
   "text": "This submarine carries tourists."
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "start_s": 150.907,
   "end_s": 159.787,
   "dur_s": 8.88,
   "text": "It is a safe and comfortable way to see the colourful fish and the plants and rocks under our seas."
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "start_s": 159.797,
   "end_s": 168.363,
   "dur_s": 8.566,
   "text": "The submarine can carry 48 people, and it has 11 large windows on each side."
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "start_s": 169.435,
   "end_s": 172.598,
   "dur_s": 3.163,
   "text": "It travels down 60 metres under the sea."
  }
 ],
 "p202": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start_s": 10.975,
   "end_s": 19.895,
   "dur_s": 8.92,
   "text": "People use different types of transport to get from one place to the next."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start_s": 19.895,
   "end_s": 33.494,
   "dur_s": 13.599,
   "text": "In Wuppertal, a city in Germany, the 'Schwebebahn' or suspension railway is very special."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start_s": 34.791,
   "end_s": 39.535,
   "dur_s": 4.744,
   "text": "The first track opened in 1901."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start_s": 40.283,
   "end_s": 50.6,
   "dur_s": 10.317,
   "text": "It is the oldest electric elevated railway with hanging cars in the world."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start_s": 50.6,
   "end_s": 57.898,
   "dur_s": 7.298,
   "text": "More than 85,000 passengers use it every day."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start_s": 58.727,
   "end_s": 68.73,
   "dur_s": 10.003,
   "text": "There are lots of special cars in Cuba, especially in Havana."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start_s": 68.73,
   "end_s": 74.15,
   "dur_s": 5.42,
   "text": "Most of them are very old."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start_s": 74.15,
   "end_s": 79.564,
   "dur_s": 5.414,
   "text": "But these yellow taxis are much newer."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start_s": 79.664,
   "end_s": 88.374,
   "dur_s": 8.71,
   "text": "They are called cocotaxis because they look like coconuts."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start_s": 88.484,
   "end_s": 93.408,
   "dur_s": 4.924,
   "text": "They are a great way of getting around."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start_s": 94.051,
   "end_s": 97.114,
   "dur_s": 3.063,
   "text": "Tourists love them!"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start_s": 98.102,
   "end_s": 109.17,
   "dur_s": 11.068,
   "text": "Tourists also like riding down the hills in Madeira, Portugal, on the Monte Toboggan."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start_s": 109.17,
   "end_s": 117.373,
   "dur_s": 8.203,
   "text": "Originally, people used these sledges to transport food and other things."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start_s": 117.518,
   "end_s": 121.935,
   "dur_s": 4.417,
   "text": "Today, they transport people."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start_s": 121.935,
   "end_s": 132.978,
   "dur_s": 11.043,
   "text": "Two 'carreiros', or sledge drivers, run next to the sledge and keep it on the street."
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "start_s": 133.901,
   "end_s": 137.757,
   "dur_s": 3.856,
   "text": "They wear special shoes."
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "start_s": 137.767,
   "end_s": 148.473,
   "dur_s": 10.706,
   "text": "When the ride gets too fast, the drivers can use their shoes to slow it down."
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "start_s": 148.682,
   "end_s": 160.894,
   "dur_s": 12.212,
   "text": "This strange form of transportation is called zorbing or globe-riding."
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "start_s": 161.08,
   "end_s": 166.6,
   "dur_s": 5.52,
   "text": "And yes, a person is inside!"
  },
  {
